isn't recommended because Windows depends on shimming for interoperability and software may become unstable or not work. Mic"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1086", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1086 PowerShell Mitigation", "tags": ["mitigation", "powershell mitigation", "t1086"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1086 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/T1086 It may be possible to remove PowerShell from systems when not needed, but a review should be performed to assess the impact to an environment, since it could be in use for many legitimate purposes and administrative funct"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M1050", "source": "mitre", "title": "M1050 Exploit Protection", "tags": ["exploit protection", "m1050", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M1050 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M1050 Deploy capabilities that detect, block, and mitigate conditions indicative of software exploits. These capabilities aim to prevent exploitation by addressing vulnerabilities, monitoring anomalous behaviors, and applying e"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1170", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1170 Mshta Mitigation", "tags": ["mitigation", "mshta mitigation", "t1170"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1170 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/T1170 Mshta.exe may not be necessary within a given environment since its functionality is tied to older versions of Internet Explorer that have reached end of life. Use application whitelisting configured to block execution of"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1035", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1035 Service Execution Mitigation", "tags": ["mitigation", "service execution mitigation", "t1035"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1035 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/T1035 Ensure that permissions disallow services that run at a higher permissions level from being created or interacted with by a user with a lower permission level. Also ensure that high permission level service binaries canno"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1042", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1042 Change Default File Association Mitigation", "tags": ["change default file association mitigation", "mitigation", "t1042"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1042 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/T1042 Direct mitigation of this technique is not recommended since it is a legitimate function that can be performed by users for software preferences. Follow Microsoft's best practices for file associations. (Citation: MSDN Fi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1206", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1206 Sudo Caching Mitigation", "tags": ["mitigation", "sudo caching mitigation", "t1206"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1206 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/T1206 Setting the <code>timestamp_timeout</code> to 0 will require the user to input their password every time <code>sudo</code> is executed. Similarly, ensuring that the <code>tty_tickets</code> setting is enabled will prevent"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1157", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1157 Dylib Hijacking Mitigation", "tags": ["dylib hijacking mitigation", "mitigation", "t1157"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1157 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/T1157 Prevent users from being able to write files to the search paths for applications, both in the folders where applications are run from and the standard dylib folders. If users can't write to these directories, then they c"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1152", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1152 Launchctl Mitigation", "tags": ["launchctl mitigation", "mitigation", "t1152"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1152 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/T1152 Prevent users from installing their own launch agents or launch daemons and instead require them to be pushed out by group policy."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M1015", "source": "mitre", "title": "M1015 Active Directory Configuration", "tags": ["active directory configuration", "m1015", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M1015 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M1015 Implement robust Active Directory (AD) configurations using group policies to secure user accounts, control access, and minimize the attack surface. AD configurations enable centralized control over account settings, logo"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M1051", "source": "mitre", "title": "M1051 Update Software", "tags": ["m1051", "mitigation", "update software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M1051 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M1051 Software updates ensure systems are protected against known vulnerabilities by applying patches and upgrades provided by vendors. Regular updates reduce the attack surface and prevent adversaries from exploiting known sec"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M1044", "source": "mitre", "title": "M1044 Restrict Library Loading", "tags": ["m1044", "mitigation", "restrict library loading"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M1044 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M1044 Restricting library loading involves implementing security controls to ensure that only trusted and verified libraries (DLLs, shared objects, etc.) are loaded into processes. Adversaries often abuse Dynamic-Link Library ("}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1492", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1492 Stored Data Manipulation Mitigation", "tags": ["mitigation", "stored data manipulation mitigation", "t1492"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1492 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/T1492 Identify critical business and system processes that may be targeted by adversaries and work to secure the data related to those processes against tampering. Ensure least privilege principles are applied to important info"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M1042", "source": "mitre", "title": "M1042 Disable or Remove Feature or Program", "tags": ["disable or remove feature or program", "m1042", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M1042 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M1042 Disable or remove unnecessary and potentially vulnerable sof