tack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0063 [2025 Poland Wiper Attacks](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0063) is a Russian state-sponsored campaign that conducted destructive cy"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0033", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0033 C0033", "tags": ["c0033", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0033 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** C0033 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0033 [C0033](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0033) was a [PROMETHIUM](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0056) campaign during which they used [StrongPity](https://attack.mitre.org/softwar"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0025", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0025 2016 Ukraine Electric Power Attack", "tags": ["2016 ukraine electric power attack", "c0025", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0025 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** 2016 Ukraine Electric Power Attack **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0025 [2016 Ukraine Electric Power Attack](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0025) was a [Sandworm Team](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0034) campaign during "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0010", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0010 C0010", "tags": ["c0010", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0010 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** C0010 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0010 [C0010](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0010) was a cyber espionage campaign conducted by UNC3890 that targeted Israeli shipping, government, aviation, energy, and healthcare organi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0040", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0040 APT41 DUST", "tags": ["apt41 dust", "c0040", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0040 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** APT41 DUST **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0040 [APT41 DUST](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0040) was conducted by [APT41](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0096) from 2023 to July 2024 against entities in Europe, Asia, and "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0002", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0002 Night Dragon", "tags": ["c0002", "campaign", "night dragon"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0002 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Night Dragon **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0002 [Night Dragon](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0002) was a cyber espionage campaign that targeted oil, energy, and petrochemical companies, along with individuals and executi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0039", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0039 Versa Director Zero Day Exploitation", "tags": ["c0039", "campaign", "versa director zero day exploitation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0039 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Versa Director Zero Day Exploitation **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0039 [Versa Director Zero Day Exploitation](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0039) was conducted by [Volt Typhoon](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1017) fr"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0014", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0014 Operation Wocao", "tags": ["c0014", "campaign", "operation wocao"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0014 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Operation Wocao **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0014 [Operation Wocao](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0014) was a cyber espionage campaign that targeted organizations around the world, including in Brazil, China, France, Ge"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0011", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0011 C0011", "tags": ["c0011", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0011 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** C0011 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0011 [C0011](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0011) was a suspected cyber espionage campaign conducted by [Transparent Tribe](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0134) that targeted students"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0049", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0049 Leviathan Australian Intrusions", "tags": ["c0049", "campaign", "leviathan australian intrusions"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0049 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Leviathan Australian Intrusions **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0049 [Leviathan Australian Intrusions](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0049) consisted of at least two long-term intrusions against victims in Australia by [Lev"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0017", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0017 C0017", "tags": ["c0017", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0017 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** C0017 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0017 [C0017](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0017) was an [APT41](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0096) campaign conducted between May 2021 and February 2022 that successfully compromis"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0026", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0026 C0026", "tags": ["c0026", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0026 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** C0026 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0026 [C0026](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0026) was a campaign identified in September 2022 that included the selective distribution of [KOPILUWAK](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0027", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0027 C0027", "tags": ["c0027", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0027 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** C0027 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0027 [C0027](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0027) was a financially-motivated campaign linked to [Scattered Spider](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1015) that targeted telecommunicatio"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0034", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0034 2022 Ukraine Electric Power Attack", "tags": ["2022 ukraine electric power attack", "c0034", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0034 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** 2022 Ukraine Electric Power Attack **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0034 The [2022 Ukraine Electric Power Attack](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0034) was a [Sandworm Team](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0034) campaign tha"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0055", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0055 Quad7 Activity", "tags": ["c0055", "campaign", "quad7 activity"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0055 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Quad7 Activity **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0055 Quad7 Activity, also known as CovertNetwork-1658 or the 7777 Botnet, is a network of compromised small office/home office (SOHO) routers. (Citation: Bitsight 7777 Botnet) (Cita"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0053", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0053 FLORAHOX Activity", "tags": ["c0053", "campaign", "florahox activity"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0053 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** FLORAHOX Activity **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0053 [FLORAHOX Activity](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0053) is conducted using a hybrid operational relay box (ORB) network, which combines two types of infrastructure: co"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0004", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0004 CostaRicto", "tags": ["c0004", "campaign", "costaricto"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0004 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** CostaRicto **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0004 [CostaRicto](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0004) was a suspected hacker-for-hire cyber espionage campaign that targeted multiple industries worldwide, with a large number bei"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0064", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0064 AI-Assisted Breach of Mexico's Government Infrastructure", "tags": ["ai-assisted breach of mexico's government infrastructure", "c0064", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0064 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** AI-Assisted Breach of Mexico's Government Infrastructure **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0064 The [AI-Assisted Breach of Mexico's Government Infrastructure](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0064) is a campaign where human ope"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-active-directory-credential-request", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Active Directory Credential Request", "tags": ["active directory credential request", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Requests for authentication credentials via Kerberos or other methods like NTLM and LDAP queries. Examples: - Kerberos TGT and Service Tickets (Event IDs 4768, 4769) - NTLM Authentication Events - LDAP Bind Requests."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-wmi-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: WMI Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "wmi creation"], "summary": "Initial construction of a WMI object, such as a filter, consumer, subscription, binding, or providers."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-group-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Group Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "group modification"], "summary": "Changes made to a group, such as membership, name, or permissions (ex: Windows EID 4728 or 4732, AWS IAM UpdateGroup). Examples: - Active Directory: - Event ID 4728: Member added to a global group. - Event ID 4732: Member added to a local group. - Azure AD: `Set-AzureADGroup -ObjectId <GroupId> -Dis"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-image-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Image Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "image modification"], "summary": "Changes made to a virtual machine image, including setting and/or control data (ex: Azure Compute Service Images PATCH)"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-pod-enumeration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Pod Enumeration", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "pod enumeration"], "summary": "Extracting a list of running or existing pods within a containerized cluster environment. Pods are the smallest deployable units in a Kubernetes cluster and typically represent an application or workload. Enumeration of pods provides insight into the structure and state of applications running in th"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-response-content", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Response Content", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "response content"], "summary": "Captured network traffic that provides details about responses received during an internet scan. This data includes both protocol header values (e.g., HTTP status codes, IP headers, or DNS response codes) and response body content (e.g., HTML, JSON, or raw data). Examples: - HTTP Scan: A web server "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-volume-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Volume Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "volume metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a cloud volume and activity around it, such as id, type, state, and size"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-response-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Response Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "response metadata"], "summary": "Contextual information about an Internet-facing resource collected during a scan, including details such as open ports, running services, protocols, and versions. This metadata is typically derived from interpreting scan results and helps build a profile of the targeted system. Examples: - Port and "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-windows-registry-key-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Windows Registry Key Deletion", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "windows registry key deletion"], "summary": "The removal of a registry key within the Windows operating system. *Data Collection Measures:* - Windows Event Logs - Event ID 4658 - Registry Key Handle Closed: Captures when a handle to a registry key is closed, which may indicate deletion. - Event ID 4660 - Object Deleted: Logs when a registry ke"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-instance-stop", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Instance Stop", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "instance stop"], "summary": "The deactivation or shutdown of a virtual machine instance within a cloud infrastructure. This action typically involves stopping a running instance, which halts its operation and releases certain associated resources, such as CPU and memory. Examples: - Google Cloud Platform (GCP): `instance.stop` "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-malware-content", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Malware Content", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "malware content"], "summary": "Code, strings, signatures, and other identifying characteristics of a malicious payload stored within a malware repository. It includes both static (file-based) and dynamic (behavioral or execution-based) components that can be analyzed for threat intelligence, detection, and prevention purposes. Ex"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-snapshot-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Snapshot Deletion", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "snapshot deletion"], "summary": "The removal of a point-in-time backup of a cloud storage volume, virtual machine (VM), or database. *Data Collection Measures:* - AWS CloudTrail - Logs `DeleteSnapshot` API calls in EC2, RDS, and EBS services. - Azure Monitor Logs - Tracks snapshot deletions via `Microsoft.Compute/snapshots/delete` "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-network-connection-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Network Connection Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "network connection creation"], "summary": "The initial establishment of a network session, where a system or process initiates a connection to a local or remote endpoint. This typically involves capturing socket information (source/destination IP, ports, protocol) and tracking session metadata. Monitoring these events helps detect lateral mo"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-access", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process Access", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process access"], "summary": "Refers to an event where one process attempts to open another process, typically to inspect or manipulate its memory, access handles, or modify execution flow. Monitoring these access attempts can provide valuable insight into both benign and malicious behaviors, such as debugging, inter-process com"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-active-directory-object-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Active Directory Object Creation", "tags": ["active directory object creation", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Creating new objects in AD, such as user accounts, groups, organizational units (OUs), or trust relationships. Logged as Event ID 5137. Examples: - User Account Creation: New user account. - Group Creation: New security/distribution group. - OU Creation: New organizational unit. - Service Account Cr"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-certificate-registration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Certificate Registration", "tags": ["certificate registration", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Certificate Registration refers to the collection and analysis of information about digital certificates, including current, revoked, and expired certificates. Sources such as Certificate Transparency logs and other public resources provide visibility into certificates issued for specific domains or"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-file-access", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: File Access", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "file access"], "summary": "To events where a file is opened or accessed, making its contents available to the requester. This includes reading, executing, or interacting with files by authorized or unauthorized entities. Examples include logging file access events (e.g., Windows Event ID 4663), monitoring file reads, and dete"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-kernel-module-load", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Kernel Module Load", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "kernel module load"], "summary": "The process of loading a kernel module into the operating system kernel. Kernel modules are object files that extend the kernel’s functionality, such as adding support for device drivers, new filesystems, or additional system calls. This action can be legitimate (e.g., loading a driver) or malicious"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-instance-enumeration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Instance Enumeration", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "instance enumeration"], "summary": "The process of retrieving or querying a list of virtual machine instances or compute instances within a cloud infrastructure. This activity provides a view of all available or running instances, typically including their associated metadata such as instance ID, name, state, and configuration details"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-file-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: File Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "file creation"], "summary": "A new file is created on a system or network storage. This action often signifies an operation such as saving a document, writing data, or deploying a file. Logging these events helps identify legitimate or potentially malicious file creation activities. Examples include logging file creation events"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-active-dns", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Active DNS", "tags": ["active dns", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "\"Domain Name: Active DNS\" data component captures queried DNS registry data that highlights current domain-to-IP address resolutions. This data includes both direct queries to DNS servers and records that provide mappings between domain names and associated IP addresses. It serves as a critical reso"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-driver-load", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Driver Load", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "driver load"], "summary": "The process of attaching a driver, which is a software component that allows the operating system and applications to interact with hardware devices, to either user-mode or kernel-mode of a system. This can include benign actions (e.g., hardware drivers) or malicious behavior (e.g., rootkits or unsi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-network-traffic-content", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Network Traffic Content", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "network traffic content"], "summary": "The full packet capture (PCAP) or session data that logs both protocol headers and payload content. This allows analysts to inspect command and control (C2) traffic, exfiltration, and other suspicious activity within network communications. Unlike metadata-based logs, full content analysis enables d"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-logon-session-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Logon Session Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "logon session metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a logon session, such as username, logon type, access tokens (security context, user SIDs, logon identifiers, and logon SID), and any activity associated within it"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-volume-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Volume Deletion", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "volume deletion"], "summary": "The removal of a cloud-based or on-premise block storage volume. This action permanently deletes the allocated storage and may result in data loss if not backed up. *Data Collection Measures:* - Cloud Logging & APIs - AWS CloudTrail Logs - `eventName: DeleteVolume` (tracks volume deletions) - Azure "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process creation"], "summary": "Refers to the event in which a new process (executable) is initialized by an operating system. This can involve parent-child process relationships, process arguments, and environmental variables. Monitoring process creation is crucial for detecting malicious behaviors, such as execution of unauthori"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-drive-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Drive Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "drive creation"], "summary": "The activity of assigning a new drive letter or creating a mount point for a data storage device, such as a USB, network share, or external hard drive, enabling access to its content on a host system. Examples: - USB Drive Insertion: A USB drive is plugged in and automatically assigned the letter `E"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-snapshot-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Snapshot Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "snapshot creation"], "summary": "The process of taking a point-in-time copy of a cloud storage volume (files, settings, configurations, etc.), virtual machine (VM), or database that can be created and deployed in cloud environments."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-storage-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Storage Modification", "tags": ["cloud storage modification", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud Storage Modification involves tracking changes made to cloud storage infrastructure, including updates to settings, permissions, or stored data. Examples include modifying object access control lists (ACLs), uploading new objects, or updating bucket policies. Examples: AWS S3: An object is upl"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-instance-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Instance Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "instance modification"], "summary": "Changes made to a virtual machine (VM) or compute instance, including alterations to its configuration, metadata, attached policies, or operational state. Such modifications can include updating metadata, attaching or detaching resource policies, resizing instances, or modifying network configuratio"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-instance-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Instance Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "instance metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about an instance and activity around it such as name, type, or status"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-storage-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Storage Deletion", "tags": ["cloud storage deletion", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud Storage Deletion refers to the removal or destruction of cloud storage infrastructure, such as buckets, containers, or directories, within a cloud environment. Monitoring this activity is critical to detecting potential unauthorized or malicious actions, such as data destruction by adversaries"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-drive-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Drive Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "drive modification"], "summary": "The alteration of a drive letter, mount point, or other attributes of a data storage device, which could involve reassignment, renaming, permissions changes, or other modifications. Examples: - Drive Letter Reassignment: A USB drive previously assigned `E:\\` is reassigned to `D:\\` on a Windows machi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-pod-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Pod Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "pod creation"], "summary": "The initial deployment or instantiation of a new pod in a containerized environment. This includes creating a pod manually, through orchestration tools (Kubernetes), or via Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) configurations. A Pod is the smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes, typically containing one or m"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-service-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Service Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "service creation"], "summary": "The registration of a new service or daemon on an operating system. *Data Collection Measures:* - Windows Event Logs - Event ID 4697 - Captures the creation of a new Windows service. - Event ID 7045 - Captures services installed by administrators or adversaries. - Event ID 7034 - Could indicate mali"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-storage-access", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Storage Access", "tags": ["cloud storage access", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud storage access refers to the retrieval or interaction with data stored in cloud infrastructure. This data component includes activities such as reading, downloading, or accessing files and objects within cloud storage systems. Common examples include API calls like GetObject in AWS S3, which r"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-storage-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Storage Creation", "tags": ["cloud storage creation", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud Storage Creation refers to the initial creation of a new cloud storage resource, such as buckets, containers, or directories, within a cloud environment. This action is critical to track as it might indicate the legitimate provisioning of resources or unauthorized actions taken by adversaries "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-active-directory-object-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Active Directory Object Modification", "tags": ["active directory object modification", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Changes to AD objects (e.g., users, groups, OUs) are logged as Event ID 5136 (Object Modification) or 5163 (Attribute Changes). Examples: - User Account: Modifying attributes (e.g., group membership, enabling/disabling accounts). - Group Membership: Adding/removing members. - OU: Changing properties"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-active-directory-object-access", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Active Directory Object Access", "tags": ["active directory object access", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Object access refers to activities where AD objects (e.g., user accounts, groups, policies) are accessed or queried. Example: Windows Event ID 4661 logs object access attempts. Examples: - Attribute Access: e.g., `userPassword`, `memberOf`, `securityDescriptor`. - Group Enumeration: Enumerating crit"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-web-credential-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Web Credential Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "web credential creation"], "summary": "Initial construction of new web credential material (ex: Windows EID 1200 or 4769)"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-container-start", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Container Start", "tags": ["container start", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "\"Container Start\" data component captures events related to the activation or invocation of a container within a containerized environment. This includes starting a previously stopped container, restarting an existing container, or initializing a container for runtime. Monitoring these activities is"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-termination", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process Termination", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process termination"], "summary": "The exit or termination of a running process on a system. This can occur due to normal operations, user-initiated commands, or malicious actions such as process termination by malware to disable security controls."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-file-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: File Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "file metadata"], "summary": "contextual information about a file, including attributes such as the file's name, size, type, content (e.g., signatures, headers, media), user/owner, permissions, timestamps, and other related properties. File metadata provides insights into a file's characteristics and can be used to detect malici"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-service-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Service Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "service modification"], "summary": "Changes made to an existing service or daemon, such as modifying the service name, start type, execution parameters, or security configurations."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-pod-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Pod Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "pod modification"], "summary": "Changes made to a pod’s configuration or control data within a containerized cluster. This can include updating settings such as resource limits, environment variables, annotations, labels, or even the containers running within the pod. Pod modifications are often executed using commands like kubect"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-command-execution", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Command Execution", "tags": ["command execution", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Command Execution involves monitoring and capturing the execution of textual commands (including shell commands, cmdlets, and scripts) within an operating system or application. These commands may include arguments or parameters and are typically executed through interpreters such as `cmd.exe`, `bas"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-drive-access", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Drive Access", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "drive access"], "summary": "Refers to the act of accessing a data storage device, such as a hard drive, SSD, USB, or network-mounted drive. This data component logs the opening or mounting of drives, capturing activities such as reading, writing, or executing files within an assigned drive letter (e.g., `C:\\`, `/mnt/drive`) or"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-firewall-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Firewall Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "firewall metadata"], "summary": "Contextual information about firewalls, including their configurations, policies, status, and other details such as names and associated rules. This metadata provides valuable insights into the operational state and configurations of firewalls, both in cloud control planes and host systems. Examples"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-service-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Service Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "service metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a service/daemon, which may include information such as name, service executable, start type, etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-instance-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Instance Deletion", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "instance deletion"], "summary": "Removal of a virtual machine (VM) or compute instance within a cloud infrastructure. This activity results in the termination and deletion of the allocated resources (e.g., CPU, memory, storage), making the instance unavailable for future use. Examples: - AWS: instance deletion involves the `Termina"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-scheduled-job-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Scheduled Job Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "scheduled job metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a scheduled job, which may include information such as name, timing, command(s), etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-windows-registry-key-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Windows Registry Key Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "windows registry key creation"], "summary": "Initial construction of a new registry key within the Windows operating system."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-file-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: File Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "file modification"], "summary": "Changes made to a file, including updates to its contents, metadata, access permissions, or attributes. These modifications may indicate legitimate activity (e.g., software updates) or unauthorized changes (e.g., tampering, ransomware, or adversarial modifications). Examples: - Content Modifications"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-host-status", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Host Status", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "host status"], "summary": "Logging, messaging, and other artifacts that highlight the health and operational state of host-based security sensors, such as Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) agents, antivirus software, logging services, and system monitoring tools. Monitoring sensor health is essential for detecting misconf"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-image-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Image Deletion", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "image deletion"], "summary": "Removal of a virtual machine image in a cloud infrastructure (ex: Azure Compute Service Images DELETE) Examples: - Azure Compute Service Image Deletion - Example: Deleting a virtual machine image using Azure CLI: `az image delete --name MyImage --resource-group MyResourceGroup` - AWS EC2 AMI (Amazon"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-snapshot-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Snapshot Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "snapshot metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a snapshot, which may include information such as ID, type, and status"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-service-enumeration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Service Enumeration", "tags": ["cloud service enumeration", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud service enumeration involves listing or querying available cloud services in a cloud control plane. This activity is often performed to identify resources such as virtual machines, storage buckets, compute clusters, or other services within a cloud environment. Examples include API calls like "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-group-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Group Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "group metadata"], "summary": "Group metadata includes attributes like name, permissions, purpose, and associated user accounts or roles, which adversaries may exploit for privilege escalation. Examples: - Active Directory: `Get-ADGroup -Identity \"Domain Admins\" -Properties Members, Description` - Azure AD: `Get-AzureADGroup -Obj"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-group-enumeration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Group Enumeration", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "group enumeration"], "summary": "Extracting group lists from identity systems identifies permissions, roles, or configurations. Adversaries may exploit high-privilege groups or misconfigurations. Examples: - AWS CLI: `aws iam list-groups` - PowerShell: `Get-ADGroup -Filter *` - (Saas) Google Workspace: Admin SDK Directory API - Azu"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-social-media", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Social Media", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "social media"], "summary": "Established, compromised, or otherwise acquired by adversaries to conduct reconnaissance, influence operations, social engineering, or other cyber threats. *Data Collection Measures:* - API Monitoring - Social media APIs (e.g., Twitter API, Facebook Graph API) can extract behavioral patterns of acco"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-active-directory-object-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Active Directory Object Deletion", "tags": ["active directory object deletion", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Object deletion in AD (e.g., user accounts, groups, OUs) is logged as Event ID 5141. Examples: - User Account: Deleted user. - Group: Deleted security/distribution group. - Organizational Unit (OU): Loss of configurations or policies. - Service Account: Disrupted operations or cover tracks. - Trust "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-container-enumeration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Container Enumeration", "tags": ["container enumeration", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "\"Container Enumeration\" data component captures events and actions related to listing and identifying active or available containers within a containerized environment. This includes information about running, stopped, or configured containers, such as their names, IDs, statuses, or associated image"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-malware-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Malware Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "malware metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a malicious payload, such as compilation times, file hashes, as well as watermarks or other identifiable configuration information"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-os-api-execution", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: OS API Execution", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "os api execution"], "summary": "Calls made by a process to operating system-provided Application Programming Interfaces (APIs). These calls are essential for interacting with system resources such as memory, files, and hardware, or for performing system-level tasks. Monitoring these calls can provide insight into a process's inten"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-application-log-content", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Application Log Content", "tags": ["application log content", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Application Log Content refers to logs generated by applications or services, providing a record of their activity. These logs may include metrics, errors, performance data, and operational alerts from web, mail, or other applications. These logs are vital for monitoring application behavior and det"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-logon-session-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Logon Session Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "logon session creation"], "summary": "The successful establishment of a new user session following a successful authentication attempt. This typically signifies that a user has provided valid credentials or authentication tokens, and the system has initiated a session associated with that user account. This data is crucial for tracking "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-script-execution", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Script Execution", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "script execution"], "summary": "The execution of a text file that contains code via the interpreter."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-container-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Container Creation", "tags": ["container creation", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "\"Container Creation\" data component captures details about the initial construction of a container in a containerized environment. This includes events where a new container is instantiated, such as through Docker, Kubernetes, or other container orchestration platforms. Monitoring these events helps"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-network-traffic-flow", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Network Traffic Flow", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "network traffic flow"], "summary": "Summarized network packet data that captures session-level details such as source/destination IPs, ports, protocol types, timestamps, and data volume, without storing full packet payloads. This is commonly used for traffic analysis, anomaly detection, and network performance monitoring."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-user-account-authentication", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: User Account Authentication", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "user account authentication"], "summary": "An attempt (successful and failed login attempts) by a user, service, or application to gain access to a network, system, or cloud-based resource. This typically involves credentials such as passwords, tokens, multi-factor authentication (MFA), or biometric validation."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-image-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Image Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "image creation"], "summary": "Initial construction of a virtual machine image within a cloud environment. Virtual machine images are templates containing an operating system and installed applications, which can be deployed to create new virtual machines. Monitoring the creation of these images is important because adversaries m"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-service-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Service Metadata", "tags": ["cloud service metadata", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud service metadata refers to the contextual and descriptive information about cloud services, including their name, type, purpose, configuration, and activity around them. This metadata is essential for understanding the roles and functions of cloud services, their operational status, and their "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-image-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Image Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "image metadata"], "summary": "contextual information associated with a virtual machine image, such as its name, resource group, status (active or inactive), type (custom or prebuilt), size, creation date, and permissions. This metadata is critical for understanding the state and configuration of virtual machine images in cloud e"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-instance-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Instance Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "instance creation"], "summary": "The initial provisioning and construction of a virtual machine (VM) or compute instance within a cloud infrastructure environment. This activity involves defining and allocating resources such as CPU, memory, storage, and networking to spin up a new compute instance. Examples: - AWS: creating an EC2"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-user-account-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: User Account Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "user account metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about an account, which may include a username, user ID, environmental data, etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-named-pipe-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Named Pipe Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "named pipe metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a named pipe on a system, including pipe name and creating process (ex: Sysmon EIDs 17-18) *Data Collection Measures:* - Windows: - Sysmon Event ID 17: Logs the creation of a named pipe. - Sysmon Event ID 18: Logs connection attempts to a named pipe. - Windows Security Event ID"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-firmware-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Firmware Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "firmware modification"], "summary": "Changes made to firmware, which may include its settings, configurations, or underlying data. This can encompass alterations to the Master Boot Record (MBR), Volume Boot Record (VBR), or other firmware components critical to system boot and functionality. Such modifications are often indicators of a"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-firewall-enumeration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Firewall Enumeration", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "firewall enumeration"], "summary": "Querying and extracting a list of available firewalls or their associated configurations and rules. This activity can occur across host systems and cloud control planes, providing insight into the state and configuration of firewalls that protect the environment. Examples: - Querying Host-Based Fire"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-module-load", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Module Load", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "module load"], "summary": "When a process or program dynamically attaches a shared library, module, or plugin into its memory space. This action is typically performed to extend the functionality of an application, access shared system resources, or interact with kernel-mode components."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-pod-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Pod Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "pod metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a pod and activity around it such as name, ID, namespace, or status"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-firewall-disable", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Firewall Disable", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "firewall disable"], "summary": "The deactivation, misconfiguration, or complete stoppage of firewall services, either on a host or in a cloud control plane. Such activity may involve turning off firewalls, modifying rules to disable protection, or deleting firewall-related configurations and activity logs. Examples: - Disabling Ho"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-passive-dns", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Passive DNS", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "passive dns"], "summary": "\"Domain Name: Passive DNS\" captures logged historical and real-time domain name system (DNS) data. This includes records of domain-to-IP address resolutions over time, enabling analysts to track the evolution of domain infrastructure, uncover historical patterns of use, and detect malicious activiti"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-user-account-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: User Account Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "user account modification"], "summary": "Changes made to an existing user, service, or machine account, including alterations to attributes, permissions, roles, authentication methods, or group memberships."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-firewall-rule-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Firewall Rule Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "firewall rule modification"], "summary": "The creation, deletion, or alteration of firewall rules to allow or block specific network traffic. Monitoring changes to these rules is critical for detecting misconfigurations, unauthorized access, or malicious attempts to bypass network protections. Examples: - Rule Creation: Adding a new rule to"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-volume-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Volume Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "volume modification"], "summary": "Changes made to a cloud volume, including its settings and control data (ex: AWS modify-volume)"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process modification"], "summary": "Changes made to a running process, such as writing data into memory, modifying execution behavior, or injecting code into an existing process. Adversaries frequently modify processes to execute malicious payloads, evade detection, or gain escalated privileges."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-user-account-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: User Account Deletion", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "user account deletion"], "summary": "The removal of a user, service, or machine account from an operating system, cloud identity management system, or directory service."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-windows-registry-key-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Windows Registry Key Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "windows registry key modification"], "summary": "Changes made to an existing registry key or its values. These modifications can include altering permissions, modifying stored data, or updating configuration settings. *Data Collection Measures:* - Windows Event Logs - Event ID 4657 - Registry Value Modified: Logs changes to registry values, includ"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-volume-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Volume Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "volume creation"], "summary": "The initial provisioning of block storage volumes in cloud or on-prem environments, typically used for data storage, backup, or workload scaling."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-user-account-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: User Account Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "user account creation"], "summary": "The initial establishment of a new user, service, or machine account within an operating system, cloud environment, or identity management system."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-container-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Container Metadata", "tags": ["container metadata", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Contextual data about a container and activity around it such as name, ID, image, or status"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-storage-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Storage Metadata", "tags": ["cloud storage metadata", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud Storage Metadata provides contextual information about cloud storage infrastructure and its associated activity. This data may include attributes such as storage name, size, owner, permissions, creation date, region, and activity metadata. It is essential for monitoring, auditing, and identify"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-service-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Service Modification", "tags": ["cloud service modification", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud service modification refers to changes made to the configuration, settings, or data of a cloud service. These modifications can include administrative changes such as enabling or disabling features, altering permissions, or deleting critical components. Monitoring these changes is critical to "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-file-deletion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: File Deletion", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "file deletion"], "summary": "Refers to events where files are removed from a system or storage device. These events can indicate legitimate housekeeping activities or malicious actions such as attackers attempting to cover their tracks. Monitoring file deletions helps organizations identify unauthorized or suspicious activities"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-service-disable", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Service Disable", "tags": ["cloud service disable", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "This data component refers to monitoring actions that deactivate or stop a cloud service in a cloud control plane. Examples include disabling essential logging services like AWS CloudTrail (`StopLogging` API call), Microsoft Azure Monitor Logs, or Google Cloud's Operations Suite (formerly Stackdrive"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-volume-enumeration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Volume Enumeration", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "volume enumeration"], "summary": "An extracted list of available volumes within a cloud environment (ex: AWS describe-volumes)"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-windows-registry-key-access", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Windows Registry Key Access", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "windows registry key access"], "summary": "The action of opening a specific Windows Registry key, typically to read its associated value. This activity can be used for system configuration, application settings retrieval, and security policies."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process metadata"], "summary": "Contextual data about a running process, which may include information such as environment variables, image name, user/owner, etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-snapshot-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Snapshot Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "snapshot modification"], "summary": "Changes made to a cloud snapshot's metadata, attributes, or control settings. These modifications may involve adjusting access permissions, changing retention policies, or altering encryption settings. *Data Collection Measures:* - AWS CloudTrail - Tracks API calls such as `ModifySnapshotAttribute`,"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-scheduled-job-creation", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Scheduled Job Creation", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "scheduled job creation"], "summary": "The establishment of a task or job that will execute at a predefined time or based on specific triggers."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-network-share-access", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Network Share Access", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "network share access"], "summary": "Opening a network share, which makes the contents available to the requestor (ex: Windows EID 5140 or 5145)"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-driver-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Driver Metadata", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "driver metadata"], "summary": "to contextual data about a driver, including its attributes, functionality, and activity. This can involve details such as the driver's origin, integrity, cryptographic signature, issues reported during its use, and runtime behavior. Examples include metadata captured during driver integrity checks,"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-instance-start", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Instance Start", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "instance start"], "summary": "The initiation or activation of a virtual machine instance within a cloud infrastructure. This action typically involves starting an existing instance that had been stopped or paused, allowing it to resume operation. Examples: - Google Cloud Platform (GCP): Starting an instance through `instance.sta"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-scheduled-job-modification", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Scheduled Job Modification", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "scheduled job modification"], "summary": "Changes made to an existing scheduled job, including modifications to its execution parameters, command payload, or execution timing."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cluster-metadata", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cluster Metadata", "tags": ["cluster metadata", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Contextual data about a cluster and activity around it such as name, namespace, age, or status"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-cloud-storage-enumeration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Cloud Storage Enumeration", "tags": ["cloud storage enumeration", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Cloud Storage Enumeration involves retrieving a list of available cloud storage infrastructure, such as buckets, containers, or objects, within a cloud environment. This activity may be performed for legitimate administrative purposes or malicious reconnaissance by adversaries seeking to identify ac"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-web-credential-usage", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Web Credentia