ing golf", "g0097", "group"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** G0097 **Type:** group **Aliases:** Bouncing Golf **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0097 [Bouncing Golf](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0097) is a cyberespionage campaign targeting Middle Eastern countries.(Citation: Trend Micro Bouncing Golf 2019) ## Techniques used - "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-group-g1029", "source": "mitre", "title": "G1029 UNC788", "tags": ["g1029", "group", "unc788"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** G1029 **Type:** group **Aliases:** UNC788 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1029 [UNC788](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1029) is a group of hackers from Iran that has targeted people in the Middle East.(Citation: Meta Adversarial Threat Report 2022) ## Techniques used"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0054", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0054 Operation Triangulation", "tags": ["c0054", "campaign", "operation triangulation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0054 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Operation Triangulation **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0054 [Operation Triangulation](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0054) is a mobile campaign targeting iOS devices.(Citation: SecureList OpTriangulation 01Jun2023) The uni"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-application-state", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Application State", "tags": ["application state", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Application State represents the operational status and lifecycle context of a mobile application at a given point in time. This includes whether the application is running in the foreground or background, its activity state, recent user interaction, and transitions between lifecycle states. Monitor"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-system-settings", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: System Settings", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "system settings"], "summary": "System Settings represent user-visible or OS-level configuration settings that influence device behavior, application permissions, connectivity, or system features. Monitoring system settings changes allows defenders to detect abnormal modifications that may indicate malicious activity or device com"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-api-calls", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: API Calls", "tags": ["api calls", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "API calls utilized by an application that could indicate malicious activity"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-application-assets", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Application Assets", "tags": ["application assets", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Application Assets represent static or packaged resources bundled with an application that may contain executable logic, configuration data, or hidden payloads. These assets may include embedded binaries, scripts, configuration files, libraries, or other resources stored within the application packa"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-protected-configuration", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Protected Configuration", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "protected configuration"], "summary": "Protected Configuration represents security-sensitive device settings, security policies, or operating system configurations that are normally restricted to administrators, system services, or device management platforms. Monitoring these configurations enables detection of adversaries attempting to"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-network-communication", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Network Communication", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "network communication"], "summary": "Network Communication captures outbound or inbound communication initiated by an application or mobile device, including the domains contacted, protocols used, and session metadata associated with the communication. Monitoring network communication enables defenders to identify command-and-control t"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-application-permission", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Application Permission", "tags": ["application permission", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "Represents the permissions, entitlements, or capability grants associated with a mobile application, including both permissions declared by the application and those granted or requested during runtime. Monitoring permission state helps defenders identify applications attempting to access protected "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-system-notifications", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: System Notifications", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "system notifications"], "summary": "System Notifications represent operating system alerts, warnings, or status messages generated in response to application actions, system state changes, or security events. These notifications may indicate potentially malicious activity or abnormal application behavior. Examples - Application reques"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-permissions-request", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Permissions Request", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "permissions request"], "summary": "System prompts triggered when an application requests new or additional permissions"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T0881", "source": "mitre", "title": "T0881 Service Stop", "tags": ["embedded", "inhibit-response-function", "linux", "network devices", "service stop", "t0881", "windows"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T0881 **Tactics:** inhibit-response-function **Platforms:** Embedded, Windows, Linux, Network Devices **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0881 Adversaries may stop or disable services on a system to render those services unavailable to legitimate users. Stopping critic"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T0836", "source": "mitre", "title": "T0836 Modify Parameter", "tags": ["embedded", "impair-process-control", "linux", "modify parameter", "t0836