ary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T0869.002 **Tactics:** command-and-control **Platforms:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0869/002 Adversaries may communicate using publish/subscribe (pub/sub) application layer protocols to avoid detection/network filtering by blending in with existing traffi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1701", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1701 Command and Scripting Interpreter", "tags": ["command and scripting interpreter", "execution", "t1701"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1701 **Tactics:** execution **Platforms:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1701 Adversaries may abuse command and script interpreters to execute commands, scripts, or binaries. These interfaces and languages provide ways of interacting with computer systems an"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1701-001", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1701.001 PowerShell", "tags": ["execution", "powershell", "t1701.001"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1701.001 **Tactics:** execution **Platforms:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1701/001 Adversaries may abuse PowerShell commands and scripts for execution. PowerShell is a powerful interactive command-line interface and scripting environment included in the W"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1701-002", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1701.002 Windows Command Shell", "tags": ["execution", "t1701.002", "windows command shell"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1701.002 **Tactics:** execution **Platforms:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1701/002 Adversaries may abuse the Windows command shell for execution. The Windows command shell (cmd) is the primary command prompt on Windows systems which is used in industrial "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T1701-004", "source": "mitre", "title": "T1701.004 Visual Basic", "tags": ["execution", "t1701.004", "visual basic"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T1701.004 **Tactics:** execution **Platforms:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1701/004 Adversaries may abuse Visual Basic (VB) for execution. VB is a programming language created by Microsoft with interoperability with many Windows technologies such as [Compo"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-T0869-001", "source": "mitre", "title": "T0869.001 DNS", "tags": ["command-and-control", "dns", "t0869.001"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** T0869.001 **Tactics:** command-and-control **Platforms:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0869/001 Adversaries may communicate using the Domain Name System (DNS) application layer protocol to avoid detection/network filtering by blending in with existing traffi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-tactic-inhibit-response-function", "source": "mitre", "title": "Tactic: Inhibit Response Function", "tags": ["inhibit response function", "inhibit-response-function", "tactic"], "summary": "The adversary is trying to prevent your safety, protection, quality assurance, and operator intervention functions from responding to a failure, hazard, or unsafe state. Inhibit Response Function consists of techniques that adversaries use to hinder the safeguards put in place for processes and prod"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-tactic-evasion", "source": "mitre", "title": "Tactic: Evasion", "tags": ["evasion", "tactic"], "summary": "The adversary is trying to avoid security defenses. Evasion consists of techniques that adversaries use to avoid technical defenses throughout their campaign. Techniques used for evasion include removal of indicators of compromise, spoofing communications, and exploiting software vulnerabilities. Ad"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-tactic-impair-process-control", "source": "mitre", "title": "Tactic: Impair Process Control", "tags": ["impair process control", "impair-process-control", "tactic"], "summary": "The adversary is trying to manipulate, disable, or damage physical control processes. Impair Process Control consists of techniques that adversaries use to disrupt control logic and cause determinantal effects to processes being controlled in the target environment. Targets of interest may include a"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0948", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0948 Application Isolation and Sandboxing", "tags": ["application isolation and sandboxing", "m0948", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0948 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0948 Restrict the execution of code to a virtual environment on or in-transit to an endpoint system."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0937", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0937 Filter Network Traffic", "tags": ["filter network traffic", "m0937", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0937 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0937 Use network appliances to filter ingress or egress traffic and perform protocol-based filtering. Configure software on endpoints to filter network traffic. Perform inline allow/denylisting of network messages based on the"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0921", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0921 Restrict Web-Based Content", "tags": ["m0921", "mitigation", "restrict web-based content"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0921 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0921 Restrict use of certain websites, block downloads/attachments, block Javascript, restrict browser extensions, etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0818", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0818 Validate Program Inputs", "tags": ["m0818", "mitigation", "validate program inputs"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0818 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0818 Devices and programs designed to interact with control system parameters should validate the format and content of all user inputs and actions to ensure the values are within intended operational ranges. These values shou"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0930", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0930 Network Segmentation", "tags": ["m0930", "mitigation", "network segmentation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0930 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0930 Architect sections of the network to isolate critical systems, functions, or resources. Use physical and logical segmentation to prevent access to potentially sensitive systems and information. Use a DMZ to contain any in"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0944", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0944 Restrict Library Loading", "tags": ["m0944", "mitigation", "restrict library loading"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0944 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0944 Prevent abuse of library loading mechanisms in the operating system and software to load untrusted code by configuring appropriate library loading mechanisms and investigating potential vulnerable software."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0915", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0915 Active Directory Configuration", "tags": ["active directory configuration", "m0915", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0915 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0915 Configure Active Directory to prevent use of certain techniques; use security identifier (SID) Filtering, etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0931", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0931 Network Intrusion Prevention", "tags": ["m0931", "mitigation", "network intrusion prevention"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0931 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0931 Use intrusion detection signatures to block traffic at network boundaries. In industrial control environments, network intrusion prevention should be configured so it will not disrupt protocols and communications responsi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0924", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0924 Restrict Registry Permissions", "tags": ["m0924", "mitigation", "restrict registry permissions"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0924 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0924 Restrict the ability to modify certain hives or keys in the Windows Registry."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0803", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0803 Data Loss Prevention", "tags": ["data loss prevention", "m0803", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0803 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0803 Data Loss Prevention (DLP) technologies can be used to help identify adversarial attempts to exfiltrate operational information, such as engineering plans, trade secrets, recipes, intellectual property, or process telemet"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0801", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0801 Access Management", "tags": ["access management", "m0801", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0801 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0801 Access Management technologies can be used to enforce authorization polices and decisions, especially when existing field devices do not provide sufficient capabilities to support user identification and authentication. ("}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0816", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0816 Mitigation Limited or Not Effective", "tags": ["m0816", "mitigation", "mitigation limited or not effective"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0816 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0816 This type of attack technique cannot be easily mitigated with preventative controls since it is based on the abuse of system features."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0950", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0950 Exploit Protection", "tags": ["exploit protection", "m0950", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0950 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0950 Use capabilities to detect and block conditions that may lead to or be indicative of a software exploit occurring."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0935", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0935 Limit Access to Resource Over Network", "tags": ["limit access to resource over network", "m0935", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0935 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0935 Prevent access to file shares, remote access to systems, unnecessary services. Mechanisms to limit access may include use of network concentrators, RDP gateways, etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0938", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0938 Execution Prevention", "tags": ["execution prevention", "m0938", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0938 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0938 Block execution of code on a system through application control, and/or script blocking."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0814", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0814 Static Network Configuration", "tags": ["m0814", "mitigation", "static network configuration"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0814 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0814 Configure hosts and devices to use static network configurations when possible, protocols that require dynamic discovery/addressing (e.g., ARP, DHCP, DNS) can be used to manipulate network message forwarding and enable va"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0927", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0927 Password Policies", "tags": ["m0927", "mitigation", "password policies"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0927 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0927 Set and enforce secure password policies for accounts."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0926", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0926 Privileged Account Management", "tags": ["m0926", "mitigation", "privileged account management"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0926 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0926 Manage the creation, modification, use, and permissions associated to privileged accounts, including SYSTEM and root."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0804", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0804 Human User Authentication", "tags": ["human user authentication", "m0804", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0804 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0804 Require user authentication before allowing access to data or accepting commands to a device. While strong multi-factor authentication is preferable, it is not always feasible within ICS environments. Performing strong us"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0920", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0920 SSL/TLS Inspection", "tags": ["m0920", "mitigation", "ssl/tls inspection"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0920 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0920 Break and inspect SSL/TLS sessions to look at encrypted web traffic for adversary activity."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0945", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0945 Code Signing", "tags": ["code signing", "m0945", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0945 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0945 Enforce binary and application integrity with digital signature verification to prevent untrusted code from executing."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0813", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0813 Software Process and Device Authentication", "tags": ["m0813", "mitigation", "software process and device authentication"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0813 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0813 Require the authentication of devices and software processes where appropriate. Devices that connect remotely to other systems should require strong authentication to prevent spoofing of communications. Furthermore, softw"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0808", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0808 Encrypt Network Traffic", "tags": ["encrypt network traffic", "m0808", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0808 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0808 Utilize strong cryptographic techniques and protocols to prevent eavesdropping on network communications."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0936", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0936 Account Use Policies", "tags": ["account use policies", "m0936", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0936 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0936 Configure features related to account use like login attempt lockouts, specific login times, etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0913", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0913 Application Developer Guidance", "tags": ["application developer guidance", "m0913", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0913 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0913 This mitigation describes any guidance or training given to developers of applications to avoid introducing security weaknesses that an adversary may be able to take advantage of."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0946", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0946 Boot Integrity", "tags": ["boot integrity", "m0946", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0946 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0946 Use secure methods to boot a system and verify the integrity of the operating system and loading mechanisms."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0805", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0805 Mechanical Protection Layers", "tags": ["m0805", "mechanical protection layers", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0805 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0805 Utilize a layered protection design based on physical or mechanical protection systems to prevent damage to property, equipment, human safety, or the environment. Examples include interlocks, rupture disk, release values,"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0951", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0951 Update Software", "tags": ["m0951", "mitigation", "update software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0951 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0951 Perform regular software updates to mitigate exploitation risk. Software updates may need to be scheduled around operational down times."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0815", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0815 Watchdog Timers", "tags": ["m0815", "mitigation", "watchdog timers"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0815 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0815 Utilize watchdog timers to ensure devices can quickly detect whether a system is unresponsive."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0809", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0809 Operational Information Confidentiality", "tags": ["m0809", "mitigation", "operational information confidentiality"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0809 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0809 Deploy mechanisms to protect the confidentiality of information related to operational processes, facility locations, device configurations, programs, or databases that may have information that can be used to infer organ"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0928", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0928 Operating System Configuration", "tags": ["m0928", "mitigation", "operating system configuration"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0928 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0928 Make configuration changes related to the operating system or a common feature of the operating system that result in system hardening against techniques."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0934", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0934 Limit Hardware Installation", "tags": ["limit hardware installation", "m0934", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0934 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0934 Block users or groups from installing or using unapproved hardware on systems, including USB devices."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0941", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0941 Encrypt Sensitive Information", "tags": ["encrypt sensitive information", "m0941", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0941 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0941 Protect sensitive data-at-rest with strong encryption."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0807", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0807 Network Allowlists", "tags": ["m0807", "mitigation", "network allowlists"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0807 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0807 Network allowlists can be implemented through either host-based files or system hosts files to specify what connections (e.g., IP address, MAC address, port, protocol) can be made from a device. Allowlist techniques that "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0817", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0817 Supply Chain Management", "tags": ["m0817", "mitigation", "supply chain management"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0817 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0817 Implement a supply chain management program, including policies and procedures to ensure all devices and components originate from a trusted supplier and are tested to verify their integrity."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0953", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0953 Data Backup", "tags": ["data backup", "m0953", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0953 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0953 Take and store data backups from end user systems and critical servers. Ensure backup and storage systems are hardened and kept separate from the corporate network to prevent compromise. Maintain and exercise incident res"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0810", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0810 Out-of-Band Communications Channel", "tags": ["m0810", "mitigation", "out-of-band communications channel"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0810 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0810 Have alternative methods to support communication requirements during communication failures and data integrity attacks. (Citation: National Institute of Standards and Technology April 2013) (Citation: Defense Advanced Re"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0947", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0947 Audit", "tags": ["audit", "m0947", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0947 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0947 Perform audits or scans of systems, permissions, insecure software, insecure configurations, etc. to identify potential weaknesses. Perform periodic integrity checks of the device to validate the correctness of the firmwa"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0802", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0802 Communication Authenticity", "tags": ["communication authenticity", "m0802", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0802 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0802 When communicating over an untrusted network, utilize secure network protocols that both authenticate the message sender and can verify its integrity. This can be done either through message authentication codes (MACs) or"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0942", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0942 Disable or Remove Feature or Program", "tags": ["disable or remove feature or program", "m0942", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0942 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0942 Remove or deny access to unnecessary and potentially vulnerable software to prevent abuse by adversaries."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0919", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0919 Threat Intelligence Program", "tags": ["m0919", "mitigation", "threat intelligence program"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0919 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0919 A threat intelligence program helps an organization generate their own threat intelligence information and track trends to inform defensive priorities to mitigate risk."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0812", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0812 Safety Instrumented Systems", "tags": ["m0812", "mitigation", "safety instrumented systems"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0812 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0812 Utilize Safety Instrumented Systems (SIS) to provide an additional layer of protection to hazard scenarios that may cause property damage. A SIS will typically include sensors, logic solvers, and a final control element t"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0917", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0917 User Training", "tags": ["m0917", "mitigation", "user training"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0917 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0917 Train users to be aware of access or manipulation attempts by an adversary to reduce the risk of successful spearphishing, social engineering, and other techniques that involve user interaction."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0932", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0932 Multi-factor Authentication", "tags": ["m0932", "mitigation", "multi-factor authentication"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0932 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0932 Use two or more pieces of evidence to authenticate to a system; such as username and password in addition to a token from a physical smart card or token generator. Within industrial control environments assets such as low"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0916", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0916 Vulnerability Scanning", "tags": ["m0916", "mitigation", "vulnerability scanning"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0916 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0916 Vulnerability scanning is used to find potentially exploitable software vulnerabilities to remediate them."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0800", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0800 Authorization Enforcement", "tags": ["authorization enforcement", "m0800", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0800 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0800 The device or system should restrict read, manipulate, or execute privileges to only authenticated users who require access based on approved security policies. Role-based Access Control (RBAC) schemes can help reduce the"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0918", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0918 User Account Management", "tags": ["m0918", "mitigation", "user account management"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0918 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0918 Manage the creation, modification, use, and permissions associated to user accounts."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0811", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0811 Redundancy of Service", "tags": ["m0811", "mitigation", "redundancy of service"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0811 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0811 Redundancy could be provided for both critical ICS devices and services, such as back-up devices or hot-standbys."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0922", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0922 Restrict File and Directory Permissions", "tags": ["m0922", "mitigation", "restrict file and directory permissions"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0922 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0922 Restrict access by setting directory and file permissions that are not specific to users or privileged accounts."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0954", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0954 Software Configuration", "tags": ["m0954", "mitigation", "software configuration"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0954 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0954 Implement configuration changes to software (other than the operating system) to mitigate security risks associated with how the software operates."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0949", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0949 Antivirus/Antimalware", "tags": ["antivirus/antimalware", "m0949", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0949 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0949 Use signatures or heuristics to detect malicious software. Within industrial control environments, antivirus/antimalware installations should be limited to assets that are not involved in critical or real-time operations."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0806", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0806 Minimize Wireless Signal Propagation", "tags": ["m0806", "minimize wireless signal propagation", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0806 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0806 Wireless signals frequently propagate outside of organizational boundaries, which provide opportunities for adversaries to monitor or gain unauthorized access to the wireless network. (Citation: CISA March 2010) To minimi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M1061", "source": "mitre", "title": "M1061 Limit Software/Package Installation", "tags": ["limit software/package installation", "m1061", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M1061 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M1061 Prevent unauthorized installation of software on ICS assets."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1004", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1004 Industroyer", "tags": ["industroyer", "s1004", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1004 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0001 [Industroyer](https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0001) is a sophisticated piece of malware designed to cause an [Impact](https://collabora"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1001", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1001 Bad Rabbit", "tags": ["bad rabbit", "s1001", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1001 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0005 [Bad Rabbit](https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0005) is a self-propagating (“wormable”) ransomware that affected the transportation secto"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1008", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1008 Stuxnet", "tags": ["s1008", "software", "stuxnet"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1008 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0010 [Stuxnet](https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0010) was the first publicly reported piece of malware to specifically target industrial cont"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1003", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1003 Conficker", "tags": ["conficker", "s1003", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1003 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0012 [Conficker](https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0012) is a computer worm that targets Microsoft Windows and was first detected in November "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1006", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1006 PLC-Blaster", "tags": ["plc-blaster", "s1006", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1006 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1006 [PLC-Blaster](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1006) is a piece of proof-of-concept malware that runs on Siemens S7 PLCs. This worm locates other Siemens S7 PLCs on the network and attem"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1005", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1005 Killdisk", "tags": ["killdisk", "s1005", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1005 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0016 In 2015 the BlackEnergy malware contained a component called KillDisk. KillDisk's main functionality is to overwrite files with random data, rendering the OS unboo"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1009", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1009 Triton", "tags": ["s1009", "software", "triton"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1009 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1009 [Triton](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1009) is an attack framework built to interact with Triconex Safety Instrumented System (SIS) controllers.(Citation: Blake Johnson, Dan Caban, M"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1002", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1002 BlackEnergy 3", "tags": ["blackenergy 3", "s1002", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1002 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0004 [BlackEnergy 3](https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0004) is a malware toolkit that has been used by both criminal and APT actors. It suppo"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1157", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1157 Fuxnet", "tags": ["fuxnet", "s1157", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1157 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1157 [Fuxnet](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1157) is malware designed to impact the industrial network infrastructure managing control system sensors for utility operations in Moscow. [Fux"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1000", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1000 ACAD/Medre.A", "tags": ["acad/medre.a", "s1000", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1000 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1000 [ACAD/Medre.A](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1000) is a worm that steals operational information. The worm collects AutoCAD files with drawings. [ACAD/Medre.A](https://attack.mitre.or"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1165", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1165 FrostyGoop", "tags": ["frostygoop", "s1165", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1165 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1165 [FrostyGoop](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1165) is a Windows-based binary written in Golang that allows for interaction with industrial control system (ICS) equipment via Modbus TCP "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1045", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1045 INCONTROLLER", "tags": ["incontroller", "s1045", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1045 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1045 [INCONTROLLER](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1045) is custom malware that includes multiple modules tailored towards ICS devices and technologies, including Schneider Electric and Omr"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-group-g1000", "source": "mitre", "title": "G1000 ALLANITE", "tags": ["allanite", "g1000", "group", "palmetto fusion"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** G1000 **Type:** group **Aliases:** ALLANITE, Palmetto Fusion **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1000 [ALLANITE](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1000) is a suspected Russian cyber espionage group, that has primarily targeted the electric utility sector within the United S"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-group-g1027", "source": "mitre", "title": "G1027 CyberAv3ngers", "tags": ["cyberav3ngers", "g1027", "group", "soldiers of soloman"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** G1027 **Type:** group **Aliases:** CyberAv3ngers, Soldiers of Soloman **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1027 The [CyberAv3ngers](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1027) are a suspected Iranian Government Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC)-affiliated APT group. The ["}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0009", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0009 Oldsmar Treatment Plant Intrusion", "tags": ["c0009", "campaign", "oldsmar treatment plant intrusion"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0009 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Oldsmar Treatment Plant Intrusion **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0009 [Oldsmar Treatment Plant Intrusion](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0009) was a cyber incident involving a water treatment facility in Florida. During th"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0020", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0020 Maroochy Water Breach", "tags": ["c0020", "campaign", "maroochy water breach"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0020 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Maroochy Water Breach **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0020 [Maroochy Water Breach](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0020) was an incident in 2000 where an adversary leveraged the local government’s wastewater control system a"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0031", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0031 Unitronics Defacement Campaign", "tags": ["c0031", "campaign", "unitronics defacement campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0031 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Unitronics Defacement Campaign **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0031 The [Unitronics Defacement Campaign](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0031) was a collection of intrusions across multiple sectors by the [CyberAv3ngers](htt"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0066", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0066 2026 U.S. Water Utilities Attacks", "tags": ["2026 u.s. water utilities attacks", "2026 water utilities attacks", "c0066", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0066 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** 2026 U.S. Water Utilities Attacks, 2026 Water Utilities Attacks **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0066 [2026 U.S. Water Utilities Attacks](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0066) was a campaign against more than 30 municipal wat"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-event-alarm", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process/Event Alarm", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process/event alarm"], "summary": "This includes a list of any process alarms or alerts produced to indicate unusual or concerning activity within the operational process (e.g., increased temperature/pressure)"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-software", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Software", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "software"], "summary": "This includes sources of current and expected software or application programs deployed to a device, along with information on the version and patch level for vendor products, full source code for any application programs, and unique identifiers (e.g., hashes, signatures)."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-history-live-data", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process History/Live Data", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process history/live data"], "summary": "This includes any data stores that maintain historical or real-time events and telemetry recorded from various sensors or devices"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-device-alarm", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Device Alarm", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "device alarm"], "summary": "This includes alarms associated with unexpected device functions, such as shutdowns, restarts, failures, or configuration changes"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-asset-inventory", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Asset Inventory", "tags": ["asset inventory", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "This includes sources of current and expected devices on the network, including the manufacturer, model, and necessary identifiers (e.g., IP and hardware addresses)"}, {"id": "owasp-cheatsheet-ai-powered-advertising-systems-security-cheat-sheet", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Cheat Sheet: AI-Powered Advertising Systems Security Cheat Sheet", "tags": ["ai-powered advertising syste