ipt Inclusion (XSSI) vulnerability allows sensitive data leakage across-origin or cross-domain boundaries. Se"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-13-reverse-tabnabbing", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 13-Reverse Tabnabbing", "tags": ["13-reverse tabnabbing", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Reverse Tabnabbing |ID | |------------| |WSTG-CLNT-13| ## Summary [Reverse Tabnabbing](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Reverse_Tabnabbing) is an attack which can be used to redirect users to"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-14-client-side-template-injection", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 14-Client-Side Template Injection", "tags": ["14-client-side template injection", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Client-side Template Injection |ID | |------------| |WSTG-CLNT-14| ## Summary Client-Side Template Injection (CSTI), also known as DOM-based Template Injection, arises when applications using client"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-15-dom-clobbering", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 15-DOM Clobbering", "tags": ["15-dom clobbering", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# DOM Clobbering |ID | |------------| |WSTG-CLNT-15| ## Summary Browsers expose some HTML elements as properties of JavaScript objects, a legacy feature known as named access: - Every element with an "}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-16-cross-site-leaks", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 16-Cross Site Leaks", "tags": ["16-cross site leaks", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Cross-Site Leaks |ID | |------------| |WSTG-CLNT-16| ## Summary Cross-site leaks (XS-Leaks) are a class of client-side issues where a page on another site learns something about a user's state on th"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-17-client-side-path-traversal", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 17-Client-side Path Traversal", "tags": ["17-client-side path traversal", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Client-side Path Traversal |ID | |------------| |WSTG-CLNT-17| ## Summary Client-side Path Traversal (CSPT) occurs when client-side code places attacker-controlled input into the path of a request t"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-18-service-workers", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 18-Service Workers", "tags": ["18-service workers", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Service Workers |ID | |------------| |WSTG-CLNT-18| ## Summary A [service worker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Service_Worker_API) is a script that the browser runs in the backgr"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-19-dns-rebinding", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 19-DNS Rebinding", "tags": ["19-dns rebinding", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# DNS Rebinding |ID | |------------| |WSTG-CLNT-19| ## Summary DNS rebinding lets a web page on an attacker's domain send requests to services that the attacker cannot reach directly, such as services"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-20-server-sent-events", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 20-Server-Sent Events", "tags": ["20-server-sent events", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Server-Sent Events |ID | |------------| |WSTG-CLNT-20| ## Summary [Server-Sent Events](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html) (SSE) let a server push a stream of events to t"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-00-api-testing-overview", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 00-API Testing Overview", "tags": ["00-api testing overview", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# API Testing Overview ## Web API Introduction A Web Application Programming Interface (API) facilitates communication and data exchange between different software systems over a network or the intern"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-01-api-reconnaissance", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 01-API Reconnaissance", "tags": ["01-api reconnaissance", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# API Reconnaissance |ID | |------------| |WSTG-APIT-01| ## Summary Reconnaissance is an important step in any pentesting engagement. This includes API pentesting. Reconnaissance significantly enhance"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-02-api-broken-object-level-authorization", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 02-API Broken Object Level Authorization", "tags": ["02-api broken object level authorization", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# API Broken Object Level Authorization |ID | |------------| |WSTG-APIT-02| ## Summary Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA) occurs when an API does not properly enforce authorization checks for ea"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-03-excessive-data-exposure", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 03-Excessive Data Exposure", "tags": ["03-excessive data exposure", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Excessive Data Exposure |ID | |------------| |WSTG-APIT-03| ## Summary Excessive data exposure occurs when an API returns more information in its responses than the client needs to display or functi"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-04-api-broken-function-level-authorization", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 04-API Broken Function Level Authorization", "tags": ["04-api broken function level authorization", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# API Broken Function Level Authorization |ID | |------------| |WSTG-APIT-04| ## Summary Broken Function Level Authorization (BFLA) occurs when an API improperly enforces restrictions on users accessi"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-05-testing-api-authentication-mechanisms", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 05-Testing API Authentication Mechanisms", "tags": ["05-testing api authentication mechanisms", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Testing API Authentication Mechanisms |ID | |------------| |WSTG-APIT-05| ## Summary APIs rely on stateless authentication mechanisms (JSON Web Tokens, OAuth 2.0 flows, API keys, and bearer tokens) "}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-06-api-rate-limiting-and-resource-consumption", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 06-API Rate Limiting and Resource Consumption", "tags": ["06-api rate limiting and resource consumption", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary":