Identification and Authentication Failures\" id: \"A07:2021\" lang: \"en\" --- {%- set parent ="}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2021-a08-2021-software-and-data-integrity-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2021): A08 2021-Software and Data Integrity Failures", "tags": ["2021", "a08 2021-software and data integrity failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "--- source: \"https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures/\" title: \"A08:2021 – Software and Data Integrity Failures\" id: \"A08:2021\" lang: \"en\" --- {%- set parent = extra.osib."}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2021-a09-2021-security-logging-and-monitoring-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2021): A09 2021-Security Logging and Monitoring Failures", "tags": ["2021", "a09 2021-security logging and monitoring failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "--- source: \"https://owasp.org/Top10/09_2021-Security_Logging_and_Monitoring_Failures/\" title: \"A09:2021 – Security Logging and Monitoring Failures\" id: \"A09:2021\" lang: \"en\" --- {%- set parent = extr"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2021-a10-2021-server-side-request-forgery-ssrf", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2021): A10 2021-Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)", "tags": ["2021", "a10 2021-server-side request forgery (ssrf)", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "--- source: \"https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_(SSRF)/\" title: \"A10:2021 – Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)\" id: \"A10:2021\" lang: \"en\" --- {%- set parent = extra.osib.docu"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2021-a11-2021-next-steps", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2021): A11 2021-Next Steps", "tags": ["2021", "a11 2021-next steps", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "--- source: \"https://owasp.org/Top10/A11_2021-Next_Steps.md/\" title: \"A11:2021 – Next Steps\" id: \"A11:2021\" lang: \"en\" --- {%- set parent = extra.osib.document ~ \".\" ~ extra.osib.version -%} {%- set o"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2021-index", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2021): index", "tags": ["2021", "index", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# OWASP Top 10 2021 介紹 歡迎來到最新版本的 OWASP Top 10！! OWASP Top 10 2021 是一個全新的名單，包含了你可以列印下來的新圖示說明，若有需要的話，你可以從我們的網頁上面下載。 在此我們想對所有貢獻了他們時間和資料的人給予一個極大的感謝。沒有你們，這一個新版本是不會出現的。**謝謝**。 ## Top 10 for 2021 有什麼新的變化？ 這次"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2021-0x00-2021-introduction", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2021): 0x00 2021-introduction", "tags": ["0x00 2021-introduction", "2021", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# Introduction ## Welcome to the OWASP Top 10 - 2021 ![OWASP Top 10 Logo](./assets/TOP_10_logo_Final_Logo_Colour.png){:class=\"img-responsive\"} Welcome to the latest installment of the OWASP Top 10! Th"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2021-0x00-notice-es", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2021): 0x00-notice.es", "tags": ["0x00-notice.es", "2021", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# Publicación Publicado el 24 de septiembre de 2021 ## Autores principales - [Andrew van der Stock](mailto:vanderaj@owasp.org) (twitter: [@vanderaj](https://x.com/vanderaj)) - [Brian Glas](mailto:bria"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-0x00-2025-introduction", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): 0x00 2025-Introduction", "tags": ["0x00 2025-introduction", "2025", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "![OWASP Logo](../assets/TOP_10_logo_Final_Logo_Colour.png) # 十大最关键 Web 应用安全风险 # 引言 欢迎阅读第 8 版 OWASP Top Ten！ 衷心感谢所有在问卷中贡献数据和观点的人。没有你们，本版不可能完成。**谢谢你们！** ## OWASP Top 10:2025 简介 * [A01:2025 - 失效的访问控制](A0"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-0x01-2025-about-owasp", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): 0x01 2025-About OWASP", "tags": ["0x01 2025-about owasp", "2025", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# 关于 OWASP Open Worldwide Application Security Project (OWASP) 是一个开放社区，致力于帮助组织开发、采购和维护可信的应用程序与 API。 在 OWASP，你可以免费、开放地获取： - 应用安全工具和标准 - 前沿研究 - 标准安全控制和库 - 关于应用安全测试、安全代码开发和安全代码审查的完整书籍 - 演示文稿和[视频](https:/"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-0x02-2025-what-are-application-security-risks", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): 0x02 2025-What are Application Security Risks", "tags": ["0x02 2025-what are application security risks", "2025", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# 什么是应用安全风险？ 攻击者可能通过应用中的多条路径对你的企业或组织造成损害。每一种路径都代表一种需要调查的潜在风险。 ![Calculation diagram](../assets/2025-algorithm-diagram.png) <table> <tr> <td> <strong>威胁主体</strong> </td> <td> <strong>攻击向量</strong> </td"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-0x03-2025-establishing-a-modern-application-security-program", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): 0x03 2025-Establishing a Modern Application Security Program", "tags": ["0x03 2025-establishing a modern application security program", "2025", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# 建立现代应用安全计划 OWASP Top Ten 系列是安全意识文档，目的是让读者关注其覆盖主题中最关键的风险。它们不是完整清单，只是起点。在本清单的早期版本中，我们建议从建立应用安全计划开始，以避免这些风险以及更多问题。本节将说明如何启动并建设现代应用安全计划。 如果你已经有应用安全计划，可以考虑使用 [OWASP SAMM（Software Assurance Maturity Model"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a01-2025-broken-access-control", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A01 2025-Broken Access Control", "tags": ["2025", "a01 2025-broken access control", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A01:2025 失效的访问控制 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Broken_Access_Control.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 失效的访问控制保持 Top Ten 第 1 位。100% 的受测应用都被发现存在某种形式的访问控制失效。该类别中值得关注的 C"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a02-2025-security-misconfiguration", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A02 2025-Security Misconfiguration", "tags": ["2025", "a02 2025-security misconfiguration", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A02:2025 安全配置错误 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Security_Misconfiguration.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 安全配置错误从上一版第 5 位上升。100% 的受测应用都被发现存在某种形式的配置错误，平均发生率为 3.00%，本风险"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a03-2025-software-supply-chain-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A03 2025-Software Supply Chain Failures", "tags": ["2025", "a03 2025-software supply chain failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A03:2025 软件供应链失效 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Vulnerable_Outdated_Components.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 该类别在 Top 10 社区问卷中排名第一，正好有 50% 的受访者将其列为第 1 位。自 2013 年 T"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a04-2025-cryptographic-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A04 2025-Cryptographic Failures", "tags": ["2025", "a04 2025-cryptographic failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A04:2025 加密机制失效 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Crypto_Failures.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 该弱点排名下降两位至第 4 位，重点关注缺少加密、加密强度不足、加密密钥泄露以及相关错误。在本风险中，几个最常见的通用弱点枚举（CWE）涉及"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a05-2025-injection", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A05 2025-Injection", "tags": ["2025", "a05 2025-injection", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A05:2025 注入 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Injection.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 注入排名从第 3 位下降两位到第 5 位，相对于 A04:2025-加密机制失效和 A06:2025-不安全设计的位置保持不变。注入是测试最充分的类别之一，10"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a06-2025-insecure-design", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A06 2025-Insecure Design", "tags": ["2025", "a06 2025-insecure design", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A06:2025 不安全设计 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Insecure_Design.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 不安全设计排名从第 4 位下滑两位到第 6 位，被 **[A02:2025-安全配置错误](A02_2025-Security_Misconf"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a07-2025-authentication-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A07 2025-Authentication Failures", "tags": ["2025", "a07 2025-authentication failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A07:2025 认证失效 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Identification_and_Authentication_Failures.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 认证失效保持第 7 位，名称略有变化，以更准确地反映本类别中的 36 个 CWE。尽管标准"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a08-2025-software-or-data-integrity-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A08 2025-Software or Data Integrity Failures", "tags": ["2025", "a08 2025-software or data integrity failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A08:2025 软件或数据完整性失效 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 软件或数据完整性失效继续位列第 8，名称从“Software *and* Data Int"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a09-2025-security-logging-and-alerting-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A09 2025-Security Logging and Alerting Failures", "tags": ["2025", "a09 2025-security logging and alerting failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A09:2025 安全日志记录和告警失效 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Security_Logging_and_Monitoring_Failures.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 安全日志记录和告警失效保持第 9 位。该类别名称略有变化，用于强调相关日志事件需"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-a10-2025-mishandling-of-exceptional-conditions", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): A10 2025-Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions", "tags": ["2025", "a10 2025-mishandling of exceptional conditions", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A10:2025 异常条件处理不当 ![icon](../assets/TOP_10_Icons_Final_Mishandling_of_Exceptional_Conditions.png){: style=\"height:80px;width:80px\" align=\"right\"} ## 背景 异常条件处理不当是 2025 年新增类别。该类别包含 24 个 CWE，关注错误处理不当、逻"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-readme-cs", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): README-cs", "tags": ["2025", "owasp", "readme-cs", "top10"], "summary": "# OWASP Top 10 - Czech (cs) This file is bilingual: English first, then Czech (Česky níže). --- ## English This directory contains a community-driven Czech translation of the **OWASP Top 10 - 2025** d"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-x01-2025-next-steps", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): X01 2025-Next Steps", "tags": ["2025", "owasp", "top10", "x01 2025-next steps"], "summary": "# 下一步 按照设计，OWASP Top 10 天然只覆盖十个最重要的风险。每一版 OWASP Top 10 都会认真考虑一些“临门一脚”的风险是否纳入，但最终它们没有入选。其他风险更普遍、影响也更大。 以下三个问题非常值得识别和修复，尤其适合正在建设成熟 AppSec 计划的组织、安全咨询公司，或希望扩展产品覆盖范围的工具厂商。 ## X01:2025 应用韧性不足 { #x012025-lac"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-2025-index", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10 (2025): index", "tags": ["2025", "index", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# OWASP Top 10:2025 欢迎阅读 OWASP Top 10:2025 发布版。 OWASP Top 10 是面向开发人员和 Web 应用安全从业者的标准安全意识文档。它代表了业界对 Web 应用最关键安全风险的广泛共识。 ## 关于本次发布 这是 OWASP Top 10 的 **2025** 版本。本版本根据最新数据和安全趋势进行了更新。 ## 主项目页面 [主项目页面](htt"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x01-frontispiece", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x01 Frontispiece", "tags": ["0x01 frontispiece", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Frontispiece ## About the Standard The Application Security Verification Standard is a list of application security requirements that architects, developers, testers, security professionals, tool ve"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x02-preface", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x02 Preface", "tags": ["0x02 preface", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Preface Welcome to the Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) Version 5.0. ## Introduction Originally launched in 2008 through a global community collaboration, the ASVS defines a compreh"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x03-what-is-the-asvs", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x03 What is the ASVS", "tags": ["0x03 what is the asvs", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# What is the ASVS? The Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) defines security requirements for web applications and services, and it is a valuable resource for anyone aiming to design, de"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x04-assessment-and-certification", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x04 Assessment and Certification", "tags": ["0x04 assessment and certification", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Assessment and Certification ## OWASP's Stance on ASVS Certifications and Trust Marks OWASP, as a vendor-neutral nonprofit, does not certify any vendors, verifiers, or software. Any assurance, trust"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x05-for-users-of-4-0", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x05 For Users Of 4.0", "tags": ["0x05 for users of 4.0", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Changes Compared to v4.x ## Introduction Users familiar with version 4.x of the standard may find it helpful to review the key changes introduced in version 5.0, including updates in content, scope,"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x10-v1-encoding-and-sanitization", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x10 V1 Encoding and Sanitization", "tags": ["0x10 v1 encoding and sanitization", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V1 Encoding and Sanitization ## Control Objective This chapter addresses the most common web application security weaknesses related to the unsafe processing of untrusted data. Such weaknesses can r"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x11-v2-validation-and-business-logic", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x11 V2 Validation and Business Logic", "tags": ["0x11 v2 validation and business logic", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V2 Validation and Business Logic ## Control Objective This chapter aims to ensure that a verified application meets the following high-level goals: * Input received by the application matches busine"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x12-v3-web-frontend-security", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x12 V3 Web Frontend Security", "tags": ["0x12 v3 web frontend security", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V3 Web Frontend Security ## Control Objective This chapter focuses on requirements designed to protect against attacks executed via a web frontend. These requirements do not apply to machine-to-mach"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x13-v4-api-and-web-service", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x13 V4 API and Web Service", "tags": ["0x13 v4 api and web service", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V4 API and Web Service ## Control Objective Several considerations apply specifically to applications that expose APIs for use by web browsers or other consumers (commonly using JSON, XML, or GraphQ"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x14-v5-file-handling", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x14 V5 File Handling", "tags": ["0x14 v5 file handling", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V5 File Handling ## Control Objective The use of files can present a variety of risks to the application, including denial of service, unauthorized access, and storage exhaustion. This chapter inclu"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x15-v6-authentication", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x15 V6 Authentication", "tags": ["0x15 v6 authentication", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V6 Authentication ## Control Objective Authentication is the process of establishing or confirming the authenticity of an individual or device. It involves verifying claims made by a person or about"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x16-v7-session-management", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x16 V7 Session Management", "tags": ["0x16 v7 session management", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V7 Session Management ## Control Objective Session management mechanisms allow applications to correlate user and device interactions over time, even when using stateless communication protocols (su"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x17-v8-authorization", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x17 V8 Authorization", "tags": ["0x17 v8 authorization", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V8 Authorization ## Control Objective Authorization ensures that access is granted only to permitted consumers (users, servers, and other clients). To enforce the Principle of Least Privilege (POLP)"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x18-v9-self-contained-tokens", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x18 V9 Self contained Tokens", "tags": ["0x18 v9 self contained tokens", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V9 Self-contained Tokens ## Control Objective The concept of a self-contained token is mentioned in the original RFC 6749 OAuth 2.0 from 2012. It refers to a token containing data or claims on which"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x19-v10-oauth-and-oidc", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x19 V10 OAuth and OIDC", "tags": ["0x19 v10 oauth and oidc", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V10 OAuth and OIDC ## Control Objective OAuth2 (referred to as OAuth in this chapter) is an industry-standard framework for delegated authorization. For example, using OAuth, a client application ca"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x20-v11-cryptography", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x20 V11 Cryptography", "tags": ["0x20 v11 cryptography", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V11 Cryptography ## Control Objective The objective of this chapter is to define best practices for the general use of cryptography, as well as to instill a fundamental understanding of cryptographi"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x21-v12-secure-communication", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x21 V12 Secure Communication", "tags": ["0x21 v12 secure communication", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V12 Secure Communication ## Control Objective This chapter includes requirements related to the specific mechanisms that should be in place to protect data in transit, both between an end-user clien"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x22-v13-configuration", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x22 V13 Configuration", "tags": ["0x22 v13 configuration", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V13 Configuration ## Control Objective The application's default configuration must be secure for use on the Internet. This chapter provides guidance on the various configurations necessary to achie"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x23-v14-data-protection", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x23 V14 Data Protection", "tags": ["0x23 v14 data protection", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V14 Data Protection ## Control Objective Applications cannot account for all usage patterns and user behaviors, and should therefore implement controls to limit unauthorized access to sensitive data"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x24-v15-secure-coding-and-architecture", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x24 V15 Secure Coding and Architecture", "tags": ["0x24 v15 secure coding and architecture", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V15 Secure Coding and Architecture ## Control Objective Many ASVS requirements either relate to a particular area of security, such as authentication or authorization, or pertain to a particular typ"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x25-v16-security-logging-and-error-handling", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x25 V16 Security Logging and Error Handling", "tags": ["0x25 v16 security logging and error handling", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V16 Security Logging and Error Handling ## Control Objective Security logs are distinct from error or performance logs and are used to record security-relevant events such as authentication decision"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x26-v17-webrtc", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x26 V17 WebRTC", "tags": ["0x26 v17 webrtc", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V17 WebRTC ## Control Objective Web Real-Time Communication (WebRTC) enables real-time voice, video, and data exchange in modern applications. As adoption increases, securing WebRTC infrastructure b"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x90-appendix-a-glossary", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x90 Appendix A Glossary", "tags": ["0x90 appendix a glossary", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Appendix A: Glossary * **Absolute Maximum Session Lifetime** – Also referred to as \"Overall Timeout\" by NIST, this is the maximal amount of time a session can remain active following authentication "}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x91-appendix-b-references", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x91 Appendix B References", "tags": ["0x91 appendix b references", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Appendix B: References The following OWASP projects are most likely to be useful to users/adopters of this standard: ## OWASP Core Projects 1. OWASP Top 10 Project: [https://owasp.org/www-project-to"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x92-appendix-c-cryptography", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x92 Appendix C Cryptography", "tags": ["0x92 appendix c cryptography", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Appendix C: Cryptography Standards The \"Cryptography\" chapter goes beyond simply defining best practices. It aims to enhance understanding of cryptography principles and encourage the adoption of mo"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x93-appendix-d-recommendations", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x93 Appendix D Recommendations", "tags": ["0x93 appendix d recommendations", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Appendix D: Recommendations ## Introduction Whilst preparing version 5.0 of the Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS), it became clear that there were a number of existing and newly sugg"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x94-appendix-e-contributors", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x94 Appendix E Contributors", "tags": ["0x94 appendix e contributors", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Appendix E - Contributors We gratefully acknowledge the contributions of the following people who have commented or opened pull requests since the the release of ASVS 4.0.0. If you are aware of any "}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x01-frontispiece", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x01 Frontispiece", "tags": ["0x01 frontispiece", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Frontispiece ## About the Standard The Application Security Verification Standard is a list of application security requirements or tests that can be used by architects, developers, testers, securit"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x02-preface", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x02 Preface", "tags": ["0x02 preface", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Preface Welcome to the Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) version 4.0. The ASVS is a community-driven effort to establish a framework of security requirements and controls that focus "}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x03-using-asvs", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x03 Using ASVS", "tags": ["0x03 using asvs", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Using the ASVS ASVS has two main goals: * to help organizations develop and maintain secure applications. * to allow security service vendors, security tools vendors, and consumers to align their re"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x04-assessment-and-certification", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x04 Assessment and Certification", "tags": ["0x04 assessment and certification", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Assessment and Certification ## OWASP's Stance on ASVS Certifications and Trust Marks OWASP, as a vendor-neutral not-for-profit organization, does not currently certify any vendors, verifiers or sof"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x10-v1-architecture", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x10 V1 Architecture", "tags": ["0x10 v1 architecture", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V1 Architecture, Design and Threat Modeling ## Control Objective Security architecture has almost become a lost art in many organizations. The days of the enterprise architect have passed in the age"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x11-v2-authentication", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x11 V2 Authentication", "tags": ["0x11 v2 authentication", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V2 Authentication ## Control Objective Authentication is the act of establishing, or confirming, someone (or something) as authentic and that claims made by a person or about a device are correct, r"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x12-v3-session-management", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x12 V3 Session management", "tags": ["0x12 v3 session management", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V3 Session Management ## Control Objective One of the core components of any web-based application or stateful API is the mechanism by which it controls and maintains the state for a user or device "}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x12-v4-access-control", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x12 V4 Access Control", "tags": ["0x12 v4 access control", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V4 Access Control ## Control Objective Authorization is the concept of allowing access to resources only to those permitted to use them. Ensure that a verified application satisfies the following hi"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x13-v5-validation-sanitization-encoding", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x13 V5 Validation Sanitization Encoding", "tags": ["0x13 v5 validation sanitization encoding", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V5 Validation, Sanitization and Encoding ## Control Objective The most common web application security weakness is the failure to properly validate input coming from the client or the environment be"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x14-v6-cryptography", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x14 V6 Cryptography", "tags": ["0x14 v6 cryptography", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V6 Stored Cryptography ## Control Objective Ensure that a verified application satisfies the following high level requirements: * All cryptographic modules fail in a secure manner and that errors ar"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x15-v7-error-logging", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x15 V7 Error Logging", "tags": ["0x15 v7 error logging", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V7 Error Handling and Logging ## Control Objective The primary objective of error handling and logging is to provide useful information for the user, administrators, and incident response teams. The"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x16-v8-data-protection", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x16 V8 Data Protection", "tags": ["0x16 v8 data protection", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V8 Data Protection ## Control Objective There are three key elements to sound data protection: Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability (CIA). This standard assumes that data protection is enforc"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x17-v9-communications", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x17 V9 Communications", "tags": ["0x17 v9 communications", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V9 Communication ## Control Objective Ensure that a verified application meets the following high level requirements: * Require TLS or strong encryption, independent of sensitivity of the content. *"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x18-v10-malicious", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x18 V10 Malicious", "tags": ["0x18 v10 malicious", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V10 Malicious Code ## Control Objective Ensure that code satisfies the following high level requirements: * Malicious activity is handled securely and properly to not affect the rest of the applicat"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x19-v11-buslogic", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x19 V11 BusLogic", "tags": ["0x19 v11 buslogic", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V11 Business Logic ## Control Objective Ensure that a verified application satisfies the following high level requirements: * The business logic flow is sequential, processed in order, and cannot be"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x20-v12-files-resources", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x20 V12 Files Resources", "tags": ["0x20 v12 files resources", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V12 Files and Resources ## Control Objective Ensure that a verified application satisfies the following high level requirements: * Untrusted file data should be handled accordingly and in a secure m"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x21-v13-api", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x21 V13 API", "tags": ["0x21 v13 api", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V13 API and Web Service ## Control Objective Ensure that a verified application that uses trusted service layer APIs (commonly using JSON or XML or GraphQL) has: * Adequate authentication, session m"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x22-v14-config", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x22 V14 Config", "tags": ["0x22 v14 config", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V14 Configuration ## Control Objective Ensure that a verified application has: * A secure, repeatable, automatable build environment. * Hardened third party library, dependency and configuration man"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x90-appendix-a-glossary", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x90 Appendix A Glossary", "tags": ["0x90 appendix a glossary", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Appendix A: Glossary - **Address Space Layout Randomization** (ASLR) – A technique to make exploiting memory corruption bugs more difficult. - **Allow list** – A list of permitted data or operations"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x91-appendix-b-references", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x91 Appendix B References", "tags": ["0x91 appendix b references", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Appendix B: References The following OWASP projects are most likely to be useful to users/adopters of this standard: ## OWASP Core Projects 1. OWASP Top 10 Project: [https://owasp.org/www-project-to"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x93-appendix-c-iot", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x93 Appendix C IoT", "tags": ["0x93 appendix c iot", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Appendix C: Internet of Things Verification Requirements This chapter was originally in the main branch, but with the work that the OWASP IoT team has done, it doesn't make sense to maintain two dif"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x01-foreword", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x01 Foreword", "tags": ["0x01 foreword", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "# Foreword Welcome to the OWASP Mobile Application Security Testing Guide. Feel free to explore the existing content, but do note that it may change at any time. New APIs and best practices are introd"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x02a-frontispiece", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x02a Frontispiece", "tags": ["0x02a frontispiece", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "# Frontispiece <img src=\"Images/owasp_mas_header.png\" width=\"100%\" /> ## About the OWASP MASTG The [OWASP Mobile Application Security Testing Guide (MASTG)](https://mas.owasp.org/MASTG/), which is par"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x02b-masvs-mastg-adoption", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x02b MASVS MASTG Adoption", "tags": ["0x02b masvs mastg adoption", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "# OWASP MASVS and MASTG Adoption The OWASP MASVS and MASTG are trusted by the following platform providers and standardization, governmental and educational institutions. ## Mobile Platform Providers "}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x02c-acknowledgements", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x02c Acknowledgements", "tags": ["0x02c acknowledgements", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "# Acknowledgments ## Contributors All of our contributors are listed in the Contributing section of the OWASP MAS website: <https://mas.owasp.org/contributing/> ## MAS Advocates Being a \"MAS Advocate\""}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x03-overview", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x03 Overview", "tags": ["0x03 overview", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "# Introduction to the OWASP Mobile Application Security Project New technology always introduces new security risks, and security concerns for mobile apps differ from traditional desktop software in i"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x04a-mobile-app-taxonomy", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x04a Mobile App Taxonomy", "tags": ["0x04a mobile app taxonomy", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "--- platform: generic --- # Mobile Application Taxonomy When we use the term \"mobile application\" or \"mobile app,\" we are referring to a self-contained computer program designed to execute on a mobile"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x04b-mobile-app-security-testing", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x04b Mobile App Security Testing", "tags": ["0x04b mobile app security testing", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "--- platform: generic --- # Mobile Application Security Testing In the following sections we'll provide a brief overview of general security testing principles and key terminology. The concepts introd"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x04c-tampering-and-reverse-engineering", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x04c Tampering and Reverse Engineering", "tags": ["0x04c tampering and reverse engineering", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-RESILIENCE platform: generic --- # Mobile App Tampering and Reverse Engineering For a long time, reverse engineering and tampering techniques have belonged to the realm of cr"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-0x04e-testing-authentication-and-session-management", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG: 0x04e Testing Authentication and Session Management", "tags": ["0x04e testing authentication and session management", "mastg", "mobile", "owasp", "testing"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-AUTH platform: generic --- # Mobile App Authentication 