ge", "mastg", "mastg know 0098", "mobile", "owasp"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-STORAGE platform: ios title: User Interface Components --- Entering sensitive information when, for example, registering an account or making payments, is an essential part o"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-know-0099", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Knowledge: MASTG KNOW 0099", "tags": ["knowledge", "mastg", "mastg know 0099", "mobile", "owasp"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-STORAGE platform: ios title: Screenshots --- Manufacturers want to provide device users with an aesthetically pleasing effect when an application is started or exited, so the"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-know-0100", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Knowledge: MASTG KNOW 0100", "tags": ["knowledge", "mastg", "mastg know 0100", "mobile", "owasp"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-STORAGE platform: ios title: Keyboard Cache --- Several options, such as autocorrect and spell check, are available to users to simplify keyboard input and are cached by defa"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-know-0101", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Knowledge: MASTG KNOW 0101", "tags": ["knowledge", "mastg", "mastg know 0101", "mobile", "owasp"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-STORAGE platform: ios title: Logs --- Logging is commonly used during development and troubleshooting to record runtime behavior, errors, and operational events. Depending on"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-know-0102", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Knowledge: MASTG KNOW 0102", "tags": ["knowledge", "mastg", "mastg know 0102", "mobile", "owasp"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-STORAGE platform: ios title: Backups --- iOS includes auto-backup features that create copies of the data stored on the device. You can make iOS backups from your host comput"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-know-0103", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Knowledge: MASTG KNOW 0103", "tags": ["knowledge", "mastg", "mastg know 0103", "mobile", "owasp"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-STORAGE platform: ios title: Process Memory --- Analyzing memory can help developers to identify the root causes of problems such as application crashes. However, it can also"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-know-0108", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Knowledge: MASTG KNOW 0108", "tags": ["knowledge", "mastg", "mastg know 0108", "mobile", "owasp"], "summary": "--- masvs_category: MASVS-STORAGE platform: ios title: App Sandbox Directories --- On iOS, each application gets a sandboxed folder to store its data. As per the iOS security model, an application's s"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0001", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0001", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0001", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Accessing the Device Shell platform: android --- One of the most common things you do when testing an app is accessing the device shell. In this section, we'll see how to access the Android"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0002", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0002", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0002", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Host-Device Data Transfer platform: android --- ## Using @MASTG-TOOL-0004 You can copy files to and from a device by using the @MASTG-TOOL-0004 commands `adb pull <remote> <local>` and `adb"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0003", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0003", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0003", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Obtaining and Extracting Apps platform: android --- There are several ways of extracting APK files from a device. You will need to decide which one is the easiest method, depending on wheth"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0004", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0004", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0004", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Repackaging Apps platform: android --- If you need to test on a non-jailbroken device, you should learn how to repackage an app to enable dynamic testing on it. Use a computer to perform al"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0005", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0005", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0005", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Installing Apps platform: android --- ## Basic APK Installation Use `adb install` (@MASTG-TOOL-0004) to install an APK on an emulator or connected device. The given path is the path of the "}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0006", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0006", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0006", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Listing Installed Apps platform: android --- When targeting apps that are installed on the device, you'll first have to figure out the correct package name of the application you want to an"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0007", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0007", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0007", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Exploring the App Package platform: android --- Once you have collected the package name of the application you want to target, you'll want to start gathering information about it. First, r"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0008", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0008", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0008", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Accessing App Data Directories platform: android --- Once you have installed the app, there is further information to explore, where tools like `objection` come in handy. When using objecti"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0009", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0009", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0009", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Monitoring System Logs platform: android --- On Android, you can easily inspect the log of system messages by using [`Logcat`](https://developer.android.com/tools/debugging/debugging-log.ht"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0010", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0010", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0010", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Basic Network Monitoring/Sniffing platform: android --- [Remotely sniffing all Android traffic in real-time is possible](https://blog.dornea.nu/2015/02/20/android-remote-sniffing-using-tcpd"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0011", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0011", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0011", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Setting Up an Interception Proxy platform: android --- Several tools support the network analysis of applications that rely on the HTTP(S) protocol. The most important tools are the so-call"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0012", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0012", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0012", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Bypassing Certificate Pinning platform: android --- Some applications will implement SSL Pinning, which prevents the application from accepting your intercepting certificate as a valid cert"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0013", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0013", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0013", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Reverse Engineering Android Apps platform: android --- Android's openness makes it a favorable environment for reverse engineers, offering significant advantages not available on iOS. Becau"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0014", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0014", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0014", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Static Analysis on Android platform: android --- Static analysis is a technique used to examine and evaluate the source code of a mobile application without executing it. This method is ins"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0016", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0016", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0016", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Disassembling Code to Smali platform: android --- If you want to inspect the app's smali code (instead of Java), you can [open your APK in Android Studio](https://developer.android.com/stud"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0017", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0017", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0017", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Decompiling Java Code platform: android --- When reverse-engineering an Android application, make sure to always identify all locations of interest regarding application logic and use the c"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0018", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0018", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0018", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Disassembling Native Code platform: android --- Dalvik and ART both support the Java Native Interface (JNI), which defines a way for Java code to interact with native code written in C/C++."}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0019", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0019", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0019", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Retrieving Strings platform: android --- While performing any kind of binary analysis, strings can be considered as one of the most valuable starting points, as they provide context. For ex"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0020", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0020", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0020", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Retrieving Cross References platform: android --- ## Java and Kotlin There are many RE tools that support retrieving Java cross references. For many of the GUI-based ones, this is usually d"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0021", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0021", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0021", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Information Gathering - API Usage platform: android --- The Android platform provides many built-in libraries for frequently used functionalities in applications, for example, cryptography,"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0022", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0022", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0022", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Information Gathering - Network Communication platform: android --- Most of the apps you might encounter connect to remote endpoints. Even before you perform any dynamic analysis (e.g. traf"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0023", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0023", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0023", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Reviewing Decompiled Java Code platform: android --- Following the example from @MASTG-TECH-0017, we assume that you've successfully decompiled and opened the @MASTG-APP-0003 app in @MASTG-"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0024", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0024", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0024", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Reviewing Disassembled Native Code platform: android --- Following the example from \"Disassembling Native Code\" we will use different disassemblers to review the disassembled native code. #"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0025", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0025", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0025", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Automated Static Analysis platform: android --- You should use tools for efficient static analysis. They allow the tester to focus on the more complicated business logic. A plethora of stat"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0026", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0026", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0026", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Dynamic Analysis on Non-Rooted Devices platform: android --- If you don't have access to a rooted device, you can patch and repackage the target app to load a dynamic library at startup (e."}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0027", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0027", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0027", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Get Open Files platform: android --- You can use `lsof` with the flag `-p <pid>` to return the list of open files for the specified process. See the [man page](http://man7.org/linux/man-pag"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0028", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0028", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0028", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Get Open Connections platform: android --- You can find system-wide networking information in `/proc/net` or just by inspecting the `/proc/<pid>/net` directories (for some reason, not proce"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0029", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0029", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0029", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Listing Loaded Native Libraries platform: android --- This technique describes how to identify and extract the native libraries loaded into memory by a running Android app. Unlike @MASTG-TE"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0031", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0031", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0031", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Debugging platform: android --- So far, you've been using static analysis techniques without running the target apps. In the real world, especially when reversing malware or more complex ap"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0032", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0032", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0032", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Execution Tracing platform: android --- Performing execution tracing during Android reverse engineering allows you to observe control flow and runtime behavior across the entire stack, from"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0033", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0033", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0033", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Method Tracing platform: android --- In contrast to method profiling, which tells you how frequently a method is being called, method tracing helps you determine its input and output values"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0034", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0034", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0034", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Native Code Tracing platform: android --- Native methods tracing can be performed with relative ease compared to Java method tracing. `frida-trace` is a CLI tool for dynamically tracing fun"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0035", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0035", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0035", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: JNI Tracing platform: android --- As detailed in @MASTG-TECH-0024, the first argument passed to every JNI function is a JNI interface pointer. This pointer contains a table of functions tha"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0036", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0036", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0036", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Emulation-based Analysis platform: android --- The Android emulator is based on QEMU, a generic and open-source machine emulator. QEMU emulates a guest CPU by translating the guest instruct"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0037", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0037", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0037", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Symbolic Execution platform: android --- Symbolic execution is a very useful technique to have in your toolbox, especially while dealing with problems where you need to find a correct input"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0038", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0038", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0038", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Patching platform: android --- Making small changes to the Android Manifest or bytecode is often the quickest way to fix small annoyances that prevent you from testing or reverse engineerin"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0039", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0039", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0039", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Repackaging & Re-Signing platform: android --- ## Repackaging You can easily repackage an app by doing the following: ```bash cd UnCrackable-Level1 apktool b zipalign -v 4 dist/UnCrackable-"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0040", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0040", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0040", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Waiting for the Debugger platform: android --- The @MASTG-APP-0003 is not stupid: it notices that it has been run in debuggable mode and reacts by shutting down. A modal dialog is shown imm"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0041", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0041", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0041", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Library Injection platform: android --- In the previous section, we learned about patching application code to assist in our analysis, but this approach has several limitations. For instanc"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0042", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0042", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0042", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Getting Loaded Classes and Methods Dynamically platform: android --- You can use the command `Java` in the Frida CLI to access the Java runtime and retrieve information from the running app"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0043", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0043", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0043", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Method Hooking platform: android --- ## Xposed Let's assume you're testing an app that's stubbornly quitting on your rooted device. You decompile the app and find the following highly suspe"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0044", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0044", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0044", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Process Exploration platform: android --- When testing an app, process exploration can provide the tester with deep insights into the app's process memory. It can be achieved via runtime in"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0045", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0045", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0045", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Runtime Reverse Engineering platform: android --- Runtime reverse engineering can be seen as the on-the-fly version of reverse engineering, where you don't have the binary data on your host"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0100", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0100", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0100", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Logging Sensitive Data from Network Traffic platform: android --- @MASTG-TOOL-0097 can be used to intercept network traffic from Android apps. This technique is useful for identifying sensi"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0108", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0108", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0108", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Taint Analysis platform: android --- Taint analysis is an information flow analysis technique that tracks the flow of sensitive information within a program. For example, it can determine w"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0109", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0109", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0109", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Intercepting Flutter HTTPS Traffic platform: android --- Flutter is an open-source UI software development kit (SDK) created by Google. It is used to build natively compiled applications fo"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0116", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0116", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0116", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Obtaining Information about the APK Signature platform: android --- ## Verify APK Signatures @MASTG-TOOL-0123 can be used to verify APK signatures: ```bash $ apksigner verify --verbose exam"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0117", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0117", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0117", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Obtaining Information from the AndroidManifest platform: android --- The [AndroidManifest.xml](../../Document/0x05a-Platform-Overview.md) file is a critical component of any Android applica"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0126", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0126", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0126", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Obtaining App Permissions platform: android --- Android permissions are declared in the `AndroidManifest.xml` file using the `<uses-permission>` tag. You can use multiple tools to view them"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0127", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0127", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0127", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Inspecting an App's Backup Data platform: android --- You can inspect an Android app's backup data to verify that sensitive data is not included in the backup. This technique is useful for "}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0128", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0128", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0128", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Performing a Backup and Restore of App Data platform: android --- ## Using the Backup Manager (via @MASTG-TOOL-0004 shell) Run [Backup Manager (`adb shell bmgr`)](https://developer.android."}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0129", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0129", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0129", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Verifying Android Dependencies at Runtime platform: android --- > The preferred techniques for analyzing dependencies are @MASTG-TECH-0131 and @MASTG-TECH-0130. This technique, which is des"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0130", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0130", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0130", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Software Composition Analysis (SCA) of Android Dependencies by Creating a SBOM platform: android --- @MASTG-TOOL-0134 can be used to create a so-called Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) in "}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0131", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: MASTG TECH 0131", "tags": ["mastg", "mastg tech 0131", "mobile", "owasp", "technique"], "summary": "--- title: Software Composition Analysis (SCA) of Android Dependencies at Build Time platform: android --- Modern Android applications rely heavily on third-party libraries, making dependency security"}, {"id": "owasp-mastg-mastg-tech-0140", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP MASTG Technique: