:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0138\n\n[OLDBAIT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0138) is a credential harvester used by [APT28](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0007). (Citation: FireEye APT28) (Citation: FireEye APT28 January 2017)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1555.003 Credentials from Web Browsers\n- T1071.003 Mail Protocols\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1555 Credentials from Password Stores\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0606": "# S0606 Bad Rabbit\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0606\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0606\n\n[Bad Rabbit](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0606) is a self-propagating ransomware that affected the Ukrainian transportation sector in 2017. [Bad Rabbit](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0606) has also targeted organizations and consumers in Russia. (Citation: Secure List Bad Rabbit)(Citation: ESET Bad Rabbit)(Citation: Dragos Apr 2019)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1486 Data Encrypted for Impact\n- T1110.003 Password Spraying\n- T1495 Firmware Corruption\n- T1569.002 Service Execution\n- T1053.005 Scheduled Task\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1189 Drive-by Compromise\n- T1003.001 LSASS Memory\n- T1548.002 Bypass User Account Control\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1135 Network Share Discovery\n- T1210 Exploitation of Remote Services\n- T1218.011 Rundll32\n- T1204.002 Malicious File\n- T1106 Native API\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0050": "# S0050 CosmicDuke\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0050\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0050\n\n[CosmicDuke](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0050) is malware that was used by [APT29](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0016) from 2010 to 2015. (Citation: F-Secure The Dukes)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1003.004 LSA Secrets\n- T1048.003 Exfiltration Over Unencrypted N