ess with Token\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1497.003 Time Based Checks\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1036 Masquerading\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0277": "# S0277 FruitFly\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0277\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0277\n\nFruitFly is designed to spy on mac users  (Citation: objsee mac malware 2017).\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1027.010 Command Obfuscation\n- T1564.001 Hidden Files and Directories\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1543.001 Launch Agent\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0230": "# S0230 ZeroT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0230\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0230\n\n[ZeroT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0230) is a Trojan used by [TA459](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0062), often in conjunction with [PlugX](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0013). (Citation: Proofpoint TA459 April 2017) (Citation: Proofpoint ZeroT Feb 2017)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1548.002 Bypass User Account Control\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1027.016 Junk Code Insertion\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1001.002 Steganography\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1027.002 Software Packing\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0276": "# S0276 Keydnap\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0276\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0276\n\nThis piece of malware steals the content of the user's keychain while maintaining a permanent backdoor  (Citation: OSX Keydnap malware).\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1090.003 Multi-hop Proxy\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1555.002