odify Tools\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1560 Archive Collected Data\n- T1685.005 Clear Windows Event Logs\n- T1115 Clipboard Data\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1010": "# S1010 VPNFilter\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1010\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1010\n\n[VPNFilter](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1010) is a multi-stage, modular platform with versatile capabilities to support both intelligence-collection and destructive cyber attack operations. [VPNFilter](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1010) modules such as its packet sniffer ('ps') can collect traffic that passes through an infected device, allowing the theft of website credentials and monitoring of Modbus SCADA protocols. (Citation: William Largent June 2018) (Citation: Carl Hurd March 2019) [VPNFilter](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1010) was assessed to be replaced by [Sandworm Team](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0034) with [Cyclops Blink](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0687) starting in 2019.(Citation: NCSC CISA Cyclops Blink Advisory February 2022)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1561.001 Disk Content Wipe\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1232": "# S1232 SplatDropper\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1232\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1232\n\n[SplatDropper](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1232) is a loader that utilizes native windows API to deliver its payload to the victim environment.  [SplatDropper](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1232) has been delivered through RAR archives and used legitimate executable for DLL side-loading.  [SplatDropper](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1232) is known to be leveraged by [Mustang Panda](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0129) and was first observed utilized in 2025.\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1027.007 Dynamic API Resolution\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1070.009 Clear Persistence\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0638": "# S0638 Babuk\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0638\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0638\n\n[Babuk](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0638) is a Ransomware-as-a-service (RaaS) malware that has been used since at least 2021. The operators of [Babuk](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0638) employ a \"Big Game Hunting\" approach to targeting major enterprises and operate a leak site to post stolen data as part of their extortion scheme.(Citation: Sogeti CERT ESEC Babuk March 2021)(Citation: McAfee Babuk February 2021)(Citation: CyberScoop Babuk February 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1685 Disable or Modify Tools\n- T1049 System Network Connections Discovery\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1486 Data Encrypted for Impact\n- T1027.002 Software Packing\n- T1489 Service Stop\n- T1490 Inhibit System Recovery\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1135 Network Share Discovery\n- T1007 System Service Discovery\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1179": "# S1179 Exbyte\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1179\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1179\n\n[Exbyte](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1179) is an exfiltration tool written in Go that is uniquely associated with [BlackByte](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1043) operations. Observed since 2022, [Exbyte](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1179) transfers collected files to online file sharing and hosting services.(Citation: Symantec BlackByte 2022)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1480 Execution Guardrails\n- T1069.001 Local Groups\n- T1140 Deobfuscat