ial gain. \n (Citation: Symantec Dyre June 2015)(Citation: Malwarebytes Dyreza November 2015)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1497.001 System Checks\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1055.001 Dynamic-link Library Injection\n- T1053.005 Scheduled Task\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1027.002 Software Packing\n- T1055 Process Injection\n- T1518 Software Discovery\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1007 System Service Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0564": "# S0564 BlackMould\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0564\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0564\n\n[BlackMould](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0564) is a web shell based on [China Chopper](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0020) for servers running Microsoft IIS. First reported in December 2019, it has been used in malicious campaigns by [GALLIUM](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0093) against telecommunication providers.(Citation: Microsoft GALLIUM December 2019)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0528": "# S0528 Javali\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0528\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0528\n\n[Javali](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0528) is a banking trojan that has targeted Portuguese and Spanish-speaking countries since 2017, primarily focusing on customers of financial institutions in Brazil and Mexico.(Citation: Securelist Brazilian Banking Malware July 2020)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1555.003 Credentials from Web Browsers\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1027.001 Binary Padding\n- T1566.002 Spearphishing Link\n- T1204.001 Malicious Link\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1218.007 Msiexec\n- T1102.001 Dead Drop Resolver\n- T1204.002 Malicious File\n- T1566.001 Spearphishing Attachment\n- T1059.005 Visual Basic\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1109": "# S1109 PACEMAKER\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1109\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1109\n\n[PACEMAKER](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1109) is a credential stealer that was used by [APT5](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1023) as early as 2020 including activity against US Defense Industrial Base (DIB) companies.(Citation: Mandiant Pulse Secure Zero-Day April 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1003.007 Proc Filesystem\n- T1055.008 Ptrace System Calls\n- T1119 Automated Collection\n- T1059.004 Unix Shell\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1143": "# S1143 LunarLoader\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1143\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1143\n\n[LunarLoader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1143) is the loader component for the [LunarWeb](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1141) and [LunarMail](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1142) backdoors that has been used by [Turla](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0010) since at least 2020 including against a European ministry of foreign affairs (MFA). [LunarLoader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1143) has been observed as a standalone and as a part of trojanized open-source software such as AdmPwd.(Citation: ESET Turla Lunar toolset May 2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1480 Execution Guardrails\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1137.006 Add-ins\n- T1620 Reflective Code Loading\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0127": "# S0127 BBSRAT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0127\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0127\n\n[BBSRAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0127) is malware with remote access tool functionality that has been used in targeted compromises. (Citation: Palo Alto Networks BBSRAT)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1560.002 Archive via Library\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1007 System Service Discovery\n- T1569.002 Service Execution\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1546.015 Component Object Model Hijacking\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1055.012 Process Hollowing\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0013": "# S0013 PlugX\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0013\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0013\n\n[PlugX](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0013) is a remote access tool (RAT) with modular plugins that has been used by multiple threat groups.(Citation: Lastline PlugX Analysis)(Citation: FireEye Clandestine Fox Part 2)(Citation: New DragonOK)(Citation: Dell TG-3390)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1622 Debugger Evasion\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1614 System Location Discovery\n- T1036.004 Masquerade Task or Service\n- T1091 Replication Through Removable Media\n- T1480.002 Mutual Exclusion\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1564.001 Hidden Files and Directories\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1204.002 Malicious File\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1102.001 Dead Drop Resolver\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1620 Reflective Code Loading\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1012 Query Registry\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1070.009 Clear Persistence\n- T1135 Network Share Discovery\n- T1127.001 MSBuild\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T