0268\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0268\n\n[Bisonal](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0268) is a remote access tool (RAT) that has been used by [Tonto Team](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0131) against public and private sector organizations in Russia, South Korea, and Japan since at least December 2010.(Citation: Unit 42 Bisonal July 2018)(Citation: Talos Bisonal Mar 2020)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1497 Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1137.006 Add-ins\n- T1059.005 Visual Basic\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1497.003 Time Based Checks\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1218.011 Rundll32\n- T1204.002 Malicious File\n- T1027.001 Binary Padding\n- T1566.001 Spearphishing Attachment\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1012 Query Registry\n- T1027.002 Software Packing\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1090 Proxy\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1568 Dynamic Resolution\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1036 Masquerading\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1135": "# S1135 MultiLayer Wiper\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1135\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1135\n\n[MultiLayer Wiper](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1135) is wiper malware written in .NET associated with [Agrius](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1030) operations. Observed samples of [MultiLayer Wiper](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1135) have an anomalous, future compilation date suggesting possible metadata manipulation.(Citation: Unit42 Agrius 2023)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1529 System Shutdown/Reboot\n- T1070 Indicator Removal\n- T1685.005 Clear Windows Event Logs\n- T1565.001 Stored Data Manipulation\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1485 Data Destruction\n- T1027.009 Embedded Payloads\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1490 Inhibit System Recovery\n- T1053.005 Scheduled Task\n- T1070.006 Timestomp\n- T1561.002 Disk Structure Wipe\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1685 Disable or Modify Tools\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9025": "# S9025 NOOPLDR\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9025\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9025\n\n[NOOPLDR](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9025) is a shellcode loader with XML/C# and DLL versions that has been used by [MirrorFace](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1054) to load [HiddenFace](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9023).(Citation: Trend Micro Earth Kasha NOV 2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1055 Process Injection\n- T1127.001 MSBuild\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1564 Hide Artifacts\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1027.016 Junk Code Insertion\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0085": "# S0085 S-Type\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0085\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0085\n\n[S-Type](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0085) is a backdoor that was used in [Operation Dust Storm](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0016) since at least 2013.(Citation: Cylance Dust Storm)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1008 Fallback Channels\n- T1071.001 Web