ations. It is heavily obfuscated and uses multiple anti-analysis techniques. It has other variants including [Wingbird](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0176). (Citation: FinFisher Citation) (Citation: Microsoft SIR Vol 21) (Citation: FireEye FinSpy Sept 2017) (Citation: Securelist BlackOasis Oct 2017) (Citation: Microsoft FinFisher March 2018)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1134.001 Token Impersonation/Theft\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1685.005 Clear Windows Event Logs\n- T1497.001 System Checks\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1056.004 Credential API Hooking\n- T1027.002 Software Packing\n- T1055.001 Dynamic-link Library Injection\n- T1548.002 Bypass User Account Control\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1542.003 Bootkit\n- T1012 Query Registry\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1027.016 Junk Code Insertion\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1574.013 KernelCallbackTable\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0374": "# S0374 SpeakUp\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0374\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0374\n\n[SpeakUp](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0374) is a Trojan backdoor that targets both Linux and OSX devices. It was first observed in January 2019. (Citation: CheckPoint SpeakUp Feb 2019)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1053.003 Cron\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1059.006 Python\n- T1110.001 Password Guessing\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1046 Network Service Discovery\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1203 Exploitation for Client Execution\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1059 Command and Scripting Interpreter\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1049 System Network Connections Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1142": "# S1142 LunarMail\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1142\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1142\n\n[LunarMail](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1142) is a backdoor that has been used by [Turla](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0010) since at least 2020 including in a compromise of a European ministry of foreign affairs (MFA) in conjunction with [LunarLoader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1143) and [LunarWeb](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1141). [LunarMail](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1142) is designed to be deployed on workstations and can use email messages and [Steganography](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1001/002) in command and control.(Citation: ESET Turla Lunar toolset May 2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1114.001 Local Email Collection\n- T1070.008 Clear Mailbox Data\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1204.002 Malicious File\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1059.005 Visual Basic\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1001.002 Steganography\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1543 Create or Modify System Process\n- T1071.003 Mail Protocols\n- T1137.006 Add-ins\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1116": "# S1116 WARPWIRE\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1116\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1116\n\n[WARPWIRE](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1116) is a Javascript credential stealer that targets plaintext passwords and usernames for exfiltration that was used during [Cutting Edge](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0029) to target Ivanti Connect Secure VPNs.(Citation: Mandiant Cutting Edge January 2024)(Citation: Mandiant Cutting Edge Part 2 January 2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1554 Compromise Host Software Binary\n- T1048.003 Exfiltration Over Unencrypted Non-C2 Protocol\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1056.003 Web Portal Capture\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0235": "# S0235 CrossRAT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0235\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0235\n\n[CrossRAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0235) is a cross platform RAT.\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1543.001 Launch Agent\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1547.013 XDG Autostart Entries\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0072": "# S0072 OwaAuth\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0072\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0072\n\n[OwaAuth](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0072) is a Web shell and credential stealer deployed to Microsoft Exchange servers that appears to be exclusively used by [Threat Group-3390](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0027). (Citation: Dell TG-3390)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1505.003 Web Shell\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1070.006 Timestomp\n- T1560.003 Archive via Custom Method\n- T1505.004 IIS Components\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0454": "# S0454 Cadelspy\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0454\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0454\n\n[Cadelspy](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0454) is a backdoor that has been used by [APT39](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0087).(Citation: Symantec Chafer Dec 2015)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1010 Application Window Discovery\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1560 Archive Collected Data\n- T1115 Clipboard Data\n- T1123 Audio Capture\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1120 Peripheral Device Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0154": "# S0154 Cobalt Strike\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0154\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0154\n\n[Cobalt Strike](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0154) is a commercial, full-featured, remote access tool that bills itself as “adversary simulation software designed to execute targeted attacks and emulate the post-exploitation actions of advanced threat actors”. Cobalt Strike’s interactive post-exploit capabilities cover the full range of ATT&CK tactics, all executed within a single, integrated system.(Citation: cobaltstrike manual)\n\nIn addition to its own capabilities, [Cobalt Strike](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0154) leverages the capabilities of other well-known tools such as Metasploit and [Mimikatz](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0002).(Citation: cobaltstrike manual)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1090.004 Domain Fronting\n- T1548.003 Sudo and Sudo Caching\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1021.001 Remote Desktop Protocol\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1550.002 Pass the Hash\n- T1078.002 Domain Accounts\n- T1027.005 Indicator Removal from Tools\n- T1548.002 Bypass User Account Control\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1569.002 Service Execution\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1055.001 Dynamic-link Library Injection\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1197 BITS Jobs\n- T1055.012 Process Hollowing\n- T1518 Software Discovery\n- T1078.003 Local Accounts\n- T1090.001 Internal Proxy\n- T1068 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1564.010 Process Argument Spoofing\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1069.002 Domain Groups\n- T1049 System Network Connections Discovery\n- T1001.003 Protocol or Service Impersonation\n- T1134.004 Parent PID Spoofing\n- T1134.001 Token Impersonation/Theft\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1059.005 Visual Basic\n- T1055 Process Injection\n- T1007 System Service Discovery\n- T1070.006 Timestomp\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1071.004 DNS\n- T1029 Scheduled Transfer\n