perform a wide range of tasks related to penetration testing such as code execution, persistence, bypassing anti-virus, recon, and exfiltration. (Citation: GitHub PowerSploit May 2012) (Citation: PowerShellMagazine PowerSploit July 2014) (Citation: PowerSploit Documentation)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1574.007 Path Interception by PATH Environment Variable\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1620 Reflective Code Loading\n- T1552.002 Credentials in Registry\n- T1027.005 Indicator Removal from Tools\n- T1123 Audio Capture\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1574.009 Path Interception by Unquoted Path\n- T1012 Query Registry\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1552.006 Group Policy Preferences\n- T1055.001 Dynamic-link Library Injection\n- T1027.010 Command Obfuscation\n- T1134 Access Token Manipulation\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1053.005 Scheduled Task\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1574.008 Path Interception by Search Order Hijacking\n- T1558.003 Kerberoasting\n- T1087.001 Local Account\n- T1547.005 Security Support Provider\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1555.004 Windows Credential Manager\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1482 Domain Trust Discovery\n- T1003.001 LSASS Memory\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1091": "# S1091 Pacu\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1091\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1091\n\nPacu is an open-source AWS exploitation framework. The tool is written in Python and publicly available on GitHub.(Citation: GitHub Pacu)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1648 Serverless Execution\n- T1685.002 Disable or Modify Cloud Log\n- T1619 Cloud Storage Object Discovery\n- T1049 System Network Connections Discovery\n- T1654 Log Enumeration\n- T1526 Cloud Service Discovery\n- T1552 Unsecured Credentials\n- T1546 Event Triggered Execution\n- T1686.001 Cloud Firewall\n- T1069.003 Cloud Groups\n- T1098.001 Additional Cloud Credentials\n- T1555.006 Cloud Secrets Management Stores\n- T1580 Cloud Infrastructure Discovery\n- T1059.009 Cloud API\n- T1530 Data from Cloud Storage\n- T1078.004 Cloud Accounts\n- T1119 Automated Collection\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1578.001 Create Snapshot\n- T1087.004 Cloud Account\n- T1651 Cloud Administration Command\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9003": "# S9003 evilginx2\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9003\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9003\n\n[evilginx2](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9003) is an open-source adversary-in-the-middle (AiTM) attack framework based on the open-source nginx web server. [evilginx2](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9003) can be used as a reverse proxy between victims and legitimate web services to intercept and capture credentials, authentication tokens, and session cookies.(Citation: Evilginx 2 July 2018)(Citation: Breakdev Evilginx 2.1 SEP 2018)(Citation: Sophos Evilginx MAR 2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1497.003 Time Based Checks\n- T1480 Execution Guardrails\n- T1539 Steal Web Session Cookie\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1557 Adversary-in-the-Middle\n- T1185 Browser Session Hijacking\n- T1111 Multi-Factor Authentication Interception\n- T1132 Data Encoding\n- T1553.004 Install Root Certificate\n- T1090.002 External Proxy\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1598.003 Spearphishing Link\n- T1001 Data Obfuscation\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0005": "# S0005 Windows Credential Editor\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0005\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0005\n\n[Windows Credential Editor](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0005) is a password dumping tool. (Citation: Amplia WCE)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1003.001 LSASS Memory\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0357": "# S0357 Impacket\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0357\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0357\n\n[Impacket](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0357) is an open source collection of modules written in Python for programmatically constructing and manipulating network protocols. [Impacket](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0357) contains several tools for remote service execution, Kerberos manipulation, Windows credential dumping, packet sniffing, and relay attacks.(Citation: Impacket Tools)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1557.001 Name Resolution Poisoning and SMB Relay\n- T1040 Network Sniffing\n- T1558.003 Kerberoasting\n- T1558.005 Ccache Files\n- T1003.003 NTDS\n- T1569.002 Service Execution\n- T1003.001 LSASS Memory\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1003.002 Security Account Manager\n- T1570 Lateral Tool Transfer\n- T1003.004 LSA Secrets\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0100": "# S0100 ipconfig\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0100\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0100\n\n[ipconfig](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0100) is a Windows utility that can be used to find information about a system's TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, and adapter configuration. (Citation: TechNet Ipconfig)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0677": "# S0677 AADInternals\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0677\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0677\n\n[AADInternals](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0677) is a PowerShell-based framework for administering, enumerating, and exploiting Azure Active Directory. The tool is publicly available on GitHub.(Citation: AADInternals Github)(Citation: AADInternals Documentation)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1526 Cloud Service Discovery\n- T1649 Steal or Forge Authentication Certificates\n- T1556.007 Hybrid Identity\n- T1098.005 Device Registration\n- T1598.003 Spearphishing Link\n- T1552.001 Credentials In Files\n- T1484.002 Trust Modification\n- T1566.002 Spearphishing Link\n- T1069.003 Cloud Groups\n- T1136.003 Cloud Account\n- T1606.002 SAML Tokens\n- T1590.001 Domain Properties\n- T1589.002 Email Addresses\n- T1558.002 Silver Ticket\n- T1552.004 Private Keys\n- T1528 Steal Application Access Token\n- T1087.004 Cloud Account\n- T1003.004 LSA Secrets\n- T1556.006 Multi-Factor Authentication\n- T1651 Cloud Administration Command\n- T1530 Data from Cloud Storage\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1048 Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0057": "# S0057 Tasklist\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0057\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0057\n\nThe [Tasklist](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0057) utility displays a list of applications and services with their Process IDs (PID) for all tasks running on either a local or a remote computer. It is packaged with Windows operating systems and can be executed from the command-line interface. (Citation: Microsoft Tasklist)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1007 System Service Discovery\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9017": "# S9017 DCRAT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9017\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9017\n\n[DCRAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9017) is a variant of the open-source [AsyncRAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1087) developed in C# with additional capabilities such as patching Microsoft’s Antimalware Scan Interface (AMSI).(Citation: Zscaler BlindEagle DEC 2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1573.002 Asymmetric Cryptography\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1685 Disable or Modify Tools\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0508": "# S0508 ngrok\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0508\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0508\n\n[ngrok](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0508) is a legitimate reverse proxy tool that can create a secure tunnel to servers located behind firewalls or on local machines that do not have a public IP. [ngrok](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0508) has been leveraged by threat actors in several campaigns including use for lateral movement and data exfiltration.(Citation: Zdnet Ngrok September 2018)(Citation: FireEye Maze May 2020)(Citation: Cyware Ngrok May 2019)(Citation: MalwareBytes LazyScripter Feb 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1090 Proxy\n- T1567 Exfiltration Over Web Service\n- T1568.002 Domain Generation Algorithms\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1572 Protocol Tunneling\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0121": "# S0121 Lslsass\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0121\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0121\n\n[Lslsass](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0121) is a publicly-available tool that can dump active logon session password hashes from the lsass process. (Citation: Mandiant APT1)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1003.001 LSASS Memory\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0099": "# S0099 Arp\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0099\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0099\n\n[Arp](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0099) displays and modifies information about a system's Address Resolution Protocol (ARP) cache. (Citation: TechNet Arp)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1018 Remote System Discovery\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0227": "# S0227 spwebmember\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0227\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0227\n\n[spwebmember](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0227) is a Microsoft SharePoint enumeration and data dumping tool written in .NET. (Citation: NCC Group APT15 Alive and Strong)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1213.002 Sharepoint\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0363": "# S0363 Empire\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0363\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0363\n\n[Empire](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0363) is an open-source, cross-platform remote administration and post-exploitation framework that is publicly available on GitHub. While the tool itself is primarily written in Python, the post-exploitation agents are written in pure [PowerShell](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/001) for Windows and Python for Linux/macOS. [Empire](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0363) was one of five tools singled out by a joint report on public hacking tools being widely used by adversaries.(Citation: NCSC Joint Report Public Tools)(Citation: Github PowerShell Empire)(Citation: GitHub ATTACK Empire)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1125 Video Capture\n- T1021.003 Distributed Component Object Model\n- T1557.001 Name Resolution Poisoning and SMB Relay\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1482 Domain Trust Discovery\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1027.010 Command Obfuscation\n- T1136.001 Local Account\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1046 Network Service Discovery\n- T1552.001 Credentials In Files\n- T1560 Archive Collected Data\n- T1484.001 Group Policy Modification\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1115 Clipboard Data\n- T1068 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation\n- T1020 Automated Exfiltration\n- T1546.008 Accessibility Features\n- T1119 Automated Collection\n- T1555.001 Keychain\n- T1615 Group Policy Discovery\n- T1087.002 Domain Account\n- T1547.005 Security Support Provider\n- T1021.004 SSH\n- T1558.003 Kerberoasting\n- T1134.005 SID-History Injection\n- T1574.009 Path Interception by Unquoted Path\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1135 Network Share Discovery\n- T1574.008 Path Interception by Search Order Hijacking\n- T1558.001 Golden Ticket\n- T1210 Exploitation of Remote Services\n- T1569.002 Service Execution\n- T1567.001 Exfiltration to Code Repository\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1056.004 Credential API Hooking\n- T1574.007 Path Interception by PATH Environment Variable\n- T1106 Native API\n- T10