[TeamPCP Cloud Stealer](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9041) was the primary payload used by [TeamPCP](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1056) in March 2026 during early stages of a cascading supply chain campaign targeting CI/CD workflows.(Citation: Wiz Trivy Compromise MAR 2026)(Citation: Aqua Security Trivy Compromise MAR 2026)(Citation: Aqua Security Blog Trivy Compromise APR 2026)(Citation: Sysdig TeamPCP MAR 2026)(Citation: Wiz TeamPCP KICS MAR 2026)(Citation: Palo Alto TeamPCP MAR 2026)(Citation: Google AI Threat Tracker MAY 2026)(Citation: FBI TeamPCP JUL 2026)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1678 Delay Execution\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1580 Cloud Infrastructure Discovery\n- T1213.006 Databases\n- T1059.006 Python\n- T1546.018 Python Startup Hooks\n- T1657 Financial Theft\n- T1555 Credentials from Password Stores\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1548.003 Sudo and Sudo Caching\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1610 Deploy Container\n- T1613 Container and Resource Discovery\n- T1518 Software Discovery\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1546.016 Installer Packages\n- T1008 Fallback Channels\n- T1552.007 Container API\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1049 System Network Connections Discovery\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1560.001 Archive via Utility\n- T1552.003 Shell History\n- T1573.002 Asymmetric Cryptography\n- T1003.007 Proc Filesystem\n- T1528 Steal Application Access Token\n- T1213.003 Code Repositories\n- T1567.001 Exfiltration to Code Repository\n- T1555.006 Cloud Secrets Management Stores\n- T1609 Container Administration Command\n- T1020 Automated Exfiltration\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1552.001 Credentials In Files\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1543.002 Systemd Service\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1059.004 Unix Shell\n- T1119 Automated Collection\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n-