52126 Kali365 May 2026)(Citation: Huntress Kali365 Device Code June 2026)(Citation: SpyCloud Kali365 June 2026)  [Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) incorporates on-demand device code generation and mirrors the copy-paste execution tradecraft associated with ClickFix. (Citation: Huntress Kali365 Device Code June 2026) Operators have used [Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) to harvest victims' OAuth tokens and session cookies through adversary-in-the-middle (AiTM) interception, enabling account takeover.(Citation: Artic Wolf Labs Kali365 Device Code April 2026)(Citation: Artic Wolf Kali365 Device Code OAuth June 2026)(Citation: FBI IC3 Alert I-052126 Kali365 May 2026)(Citation: Huntress Kali365 Device Code June 2026)(Citation: SpyCloud Kali365 June 2026)  [Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) PHaaS was first observed in April 2026.(Citation: Artic Wolf Labs Kali365 Device Code April 2026)  [Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) has also been affiliated with other branding to include Octopi365 and Freedom365.(Citation: Huntress Kali365 Device Code June 2026)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1566.002 Spearphishing Link\n- T1683.001 Written Content\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1090 Proxy\n- T1552.001 Credentials In Files\n- T1539 Steal Web Session Cookie\n- T1528 Steal Application Access Token\n- T1557 Adversary-in-the-Middle\n- T1566.001 Spearphishing Attachment\n- T1204.001 Malicious Link\n- T1564.008 Email Hiding Rules\n- T1087.003 Email Account\n- T1550.001 Application Access Token\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1185 Browser Session Hijacking\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1204.004 Malicious Copy and Paste\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9062": "# S9062 MiniBrowse\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9062\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9062\n\n[MiniBrowse](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9062) is a custom stealer designed for the theft of credentials in browsers and passwords stores. [Mi